window.__STORIES__=[{"key":0,"title":"Jiwoo's Lucky Photo","ids":["sharp","monitor","mild","area","shade","lunchtime","powder","teammate","starry","character","bleed","still","fountain","however","defend","frame","as","search","report","sigh"],"parts":[{"en":"At nine o'clock sharp, Jiwoo got to the park. It was a mild and sunny day. Her teammate Mina waved from the soccer area. \"Today we will defend the goal,\" Mina said. Jiwoo felt a little nervous. However, she smiled and ran to the field. She wanted to play as well as her favorite cartoon character.","ko":"9시 정각에 지우는 공원에 도착했어요. 온화하고 화창한 날이었어요. 팀 동료 미나가 축구 구역에서 손을 흔들었어요. \"오늘 우리는 골대를 지킬 거야.\" 미나가 말했어요. 지우는 조금 긴장했어요. 하지만 지우는 웃으며 경기장으로 달려갔어요. 지우는 가장 좋아하는 만화 등장인물처럼 잘하고 싶었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What will Jiwoo and Mina do today?","options":["Swim in a pool","Defend the goal","Eat ice cream","Read a book"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"미나가 오늘 골대를 지킬 거라고 말했어요."},{"q":"In the story, \"mild\" day means a day that is ___.","options":["very cold","very windy","warm and nice","dark and rainy"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"mild는 '온화한, 따뜻한'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["At nine o'clock sharp, Jiwoo got to the park.","Her teammate Mina waved from the soccer area."],"sents":["At nine o'clock sharp, Jiwoo got to the park.","It was a mild and sunny day.","Her teammate Mina waved from the soccer area.","\"Today we will defend the goal,\" Mina said.","Jiwoo felt a little nervous.","However, she smiled and ran to the field.","She wanted to play as well as her favorite cartoon character."]},{"en":"The game was hard. Jiwoo fell down on the grass. Her knee did not bleed, but it hurt a little. She sat still in the shade of a big tree. The coach watched the game on a small monitor. \"You did great,\" he said. At lunchtime, the team ate rice balls near the fountain.","ko":"경기는 힘들었어요. 지우는 잔디 위에 넘어졌어요. 무릎에서 피가 나지는 않았지만 조금 아팠어요. 지우는 큰 나무 그늘에 가만히 앉아 있었어요. 코치님은 작은 모니터로 경기를 지켜보았어요. \"정말 잘했어.\" 코치님이 말했어요. 점심시간에 팀은 분수 근처에서 주먹밥을 먹었어요.","questions":[{"q":"Where did the team eat lunch?","options":["Near the fountain","In a classroom","On a bus","At home"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"점심시간에 분수 근처에서 주먹밥을 먹었어요."},{"q":"\"She sat still\" means she sat ___.","options":["and sang","and ran","and cried loudly","without moving"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"여기서 still은 '가만히 있는'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["She sat still in the shade of a big tree.","The coach watched the game on a small monitor."],"sents":["The game was hard.","Jiwoo fell down on the grass.","Her knee did not bleed, but it hurt a little.","She sat still in the shade of a big tree.","The coach watched the game on a small monitor.","\"You did great,\" he said.","At lunchtime, the team ate rice balls near the fountain."]},{"en":"After lunch, Jiwoo could not find her lucky photo. It was in a little blue frame. \"Let's search for it!\" said Mina. They looked under the benches and by the fountain. On the path, they saw white powder. \"That is just chalk for the field lines,\" Mina said. Jiwoo gave a big sigh. The photo was still lost.","ko":"점심을 먹은 후, 지우는 행운의 사진을 찾을 수 없었어요. 사진은 작은 파란 액자에 들어 있었어요. \"같이 찾아보자!\" 미나가 말했어요. 둘은 벤치 아래와 분수 옆을 살펴보았어요. 길 위에서 하얀 가루를 보았어요. \"그건 그냥 경기장 선을 그리는 분필이야.\" 미나가 말했어요. 지우는 크게 한숨을 쉬었어요. 사진은 여전히 찾지 못했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What was the white powder?","options":["Sugar","Snow","Chalk for the field lines","Flour for bread"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"미나가 그건 경기장 선을 그리는 분필이라고 했어요."},{"q":"\"Let's search for it\" means let's ___ it.","options":["look for","throw away","draw","eat"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"search는 '찾다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["It was in a little blue frame.","On the path, they saw white powder."],"sents":["After lunch, Jiwoo could not find her lucky photo.","It was in a little blue frame.","\"Let's search for it!\" said Mina.","They looked under the benches and by the fountain.","On the path, they saw white powder.","\"That is just chalk for the field lines,\" Mina said.","Jiwoo gave a big sigh.","The photo was still lost."]},{"en":"Later, a girl walked over with the blue frame. \"I found this. I will report it to the coach,\" she said. \"It's mine!\" Jiwoo said happily. Inside was a photo of Jiwoo and her grandma under a starry sky. \"Thank you so much!\" said Jiwoo. That night, she wrote a report about her busy, happy day.","ko":"나중에 한 여자아이가 파란 액자를 들고 걸어왔어요. \"이거 내가 찾았어. 코치님께 알리려고 해.\" 그 아이가 말했어요. \"그거 내 거야!\" 지우가 기쁘게 말했어요. 안에는 별이 총총한 하늘 아래 지우와 할머니가 함께 찍은 사진이 있었어요. \"정말 고마워!\" 지우가 말했어요. 그날 밤, 지우는 바쁘고 행복했던 하루에 대한 보고서를 썼어요.","questions":[{"q":"Who was in the photo with Jiwoo?","options":["Her teacher","Her coach","Mina","Her grandma"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"사진에는 지우와 할머니가 있었어요."},{"q":"A \"starry\" sky is a sky ___.","options":["with many stars","with no light","full of rain","with one cloud"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"starry는 '별이 총총한'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Later, a girl walked over with the blue frame.","That night, she wrote a report about her busy, happy day."],"sents":["Later, a girl walked over with the blue frame.","\"I found this.","I will report it to the coach,\" she said.","\"It's mine!\" Jiwoo said happily.","Inside was a photo of Jiwoo and her grandma under a starry sky.","\"Thank you so much!\" said Jiwoo.","That night, she wrote a report about her busy, happy day."]}]},{"key":1,"title":"Hana and Bean the Caterpillar","ids":["tub","blind","destroy","decrease","suppose","try","band","caterpillar","gallery","thought","toast","thousand","greatly","spread","cashier","focus","sometimes","laundry","moonlight","chili"],"parts":[{"en":"On Saturday morning, Hana made toast. She spread strawberry jam on it. Then she saw a tiny green caterpillar on the window blind. \"Hello, little friend,\" she said. She put it in a small tub with fresh leaves. \"I suppose you are hungry,\" she thought. Hana named it Bean. Sometimes Bean wiggled happily.","ko":"토요일 아침, 하나는 토스트를 만들었어요. 하나는 그 위에 딸기잼을 펴 발랐어요. 그때 창문 블라인드 위에 있는 작은 초록 애벌레를 보았어요. \"안녕, 작은 친구야.\" 하나가 말했어요. 하나는 애벌레를 신선한 잎과 함께 작은 통에 넣었어요. '배가 고플 것 같아.' 하나는 생각했어요. 하나는 애벌레에게 빈이라는 이름을 지어 주었어요. 빈은 가끔 기분 좋게 꿈틀거렸어요.","questions":[{"q":"Where did Hana find the caterpillar?","options":["In her shoe","On the window blind","Under the bed","In the toast"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"애벌레는 창문 블라인드 위에 있었어요."},{"q":"\"She spread strawberry jam\" means she ___ the jam.","options":["ate all of","threw away","put a thin layer of","bought"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"spread는 '펴 바르다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["On Saturday morning, Hana made toast.","She put it in a small tub with fresh leaves."],"sents":["On Saturday morning, Hana made toast.","She spread strawberry jam on it.","Then she saw a tiny green caterpillar on the window blind.","\"Hello, little friend,\" she said.","She put it in a small tub with fresh leaves.","\"I suppose you are hungry,\" she thought.","Hana named it Bean.","Sometimes Bean wiggled happily."]},{"en":"Hana's mom was doing the laundry. \"Can Bean come to the art gallery with us?\" Hana asked. \"Yes, but focus on the paintings,\" Mom said. The gallery had a thousand pictures. One picture showed a big yellow butterfly. Hana liked it greatly. \"Bean will be a butterfly someday,\" she whispered to the tub.","ko":"하나의 엄마는 빨래를 하고 있었어요. \"빈도 우리랑 미술관에 같이 가도 돼요?\" 하나가 물었어요. \"그래, 하지만 그림에 집중하렴.\" 엄마가 말했어요. 미술관에는 그림이 천 개나 있었어요. 한 그림에는 큰 노란 나비가 있었어요. 하나는 그 그림이 정말 좋았어요. \"빈도 언젠가 나비가 될 거야.\" 하나는 통에 대고 속삭였어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did one picture in the gallery show?","options":["A big yellow butterfly","A red car","A cat","A snowman"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"한 그림에 큰 노란 나비가 있었어요."},{"q":"\"Focus on the paintings\" means ___ the paintings.","options":["paint over","sell","pay close attention to","hide"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"focus는 '집중하다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Hana's mom was doing the laundry.","The gallery had a thousand pictures."],"sents":["Hana's mom was doing the laundry.","\"Can Bean come to the art gallery with us?\" Hana asked.","\"Yes, but focus on the paintings,\" Mom said.","The gallery had a thousand pictures.","One picture showed a big yellow butterfly.","Hana liked it greatly.","\"Bean will be a butterfly someday,\" she whispered to the tub."]},{"en":"After the gallery, they went to the market. The cashier smiled at Bean. \"Try this chili cracker,\" she said to Hana. It was very hot! Hana drank lots of water. Then a boy ran by and almost knocked over the tub. \"Be careful! Please don't destroy his home!\" Hana said. The boy said sorry.","ko":"미술관에 다녀온 후, 그들은 시장에 갔어요. 계산원이 빈을 보고 웃었어요. \"이 고추 과자 한번 먹어 봐.\" 계산원이 하나에게 말했어요. 정말 매웠어요! 하나는 물을 많이 마셨어요. 그때 한 남자아이가 뛰어가다가 통을 거의 넘어뜨릴 뻔했어요. \"조심해! 빈의 집을 부수지 말아 줘!\" 하나가 말했어요. 남자아이는 미안하다고 했어요.","questions":[{"q":"How did the chili cracker taste?","options":["Sweet","Salty","Sour","Very hot"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"고추 과자는 정말 매웠어요."},{"q":"\"Don't destroy his home\" means don't ___ his home.","options":["clean","break","paint","visit"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"destroy는 '파괴하다, 부수다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["After the gallery, they went to the market.","The cashier smiled at Bean."],"sents":["After the gallery, they went to the market.","The cashier smiled at Bean.","\"Try this chili cracker,\" she said to Hana.","It was very hot!","Hana drank lots of water.","Then a boy ran by and almost knocked over the tub.","\"Be careful!","Please don't destroy his home!\" Hana said.","The boy said sorry."]},{"en":"At home, Bean ate and ate. Hana's worry began to decrease. A week later, Bean made a cocoon. One night, a little band played music outside. In the soft moonlight, Hana saw the cocoon open. A yellow butterfly came out! Then she had a new thought. \"Let's set Bean free.\" Bean flew happily away.","ko":"집에서 빈은 먹고 또 먹었어요. 하나의 걱정은 줄어들기 시작했어요. 일주일 뒤, 빈은 고치를 만들었어요. 어느 날 밤, 작은 밴드가 밖에서 음악을 연주했어요. 부드러운 달빛 속에서 하나는 고치가 열리는 것을 보았어요. 노란 나비가 나왔어요! 그때 하나에게 새로운 생각이 떠올랐어요. \"빈을 자유롭게 놓아주자.\" 빈은 행복하게 날아갔어요.","questions":[{"q":"What came out of the cocoon?","options":["A bee","A bird","A yellow butterfly","A frog"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"고치에서 노란 나비가 나왔어요."},{"q":"\"Hana's worry began to decrease\" means her worry ___.","options":["got smaller","got bigger","stayed the same","made her cry"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"decrease는 '줄다, 감소하다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["One night, a little band played music outside.","In the soft moonlight, Hana saw the cocoon open."],"sents":["At home, Bean ate and ate.","Hana's worry began to decrease.","A week later, Bean made a cocoon.","One night, a little band played music outside.","In the soft moonlight, Hana saw the cocoon open.","A yellow butterfly came out!","Then she had a new thought.","\"Let's set Bean free.\" Bean flew happily away."]}]},{"key":2,"title":"Minho's Birthday Cake Plan","ids":["reed","twice","fear","type","force","violence","quite","damage","bother","recommend","own","order","decorate","review","scar","such","batter","clinic","classical","stuffy"],"parts":[{"en":"Minho woke up with a stuffy nose. \"Achoo!\" He sneezed twice. Mom took him to the clinic. Minho had a little fear of doctors. But the doctor was quite kind. She had a small scar on her hand from cooking. \"Drink warm tea,\" she said. \"I recommend lots of sleep, too.\"","ko":"민호는 코가 막힌 채로 일어났어요. \"에취!\" 민호는 재채기를 두 번 했어요. 엄마는 민호를 병원에 데려갔어요. 민호는 의사 선생님을 조금 무서워했어요. 하지만 의사 선생님은 꽤 친절했어요. 선생님 손에는 요리하다 생긴 작은 흉터가 있었어요. \"따뜻한 차를 마시렴.\" 선생님이 말했어요. \"잠도 많이 자는 걸 권할게.\"","questions":[{"q":"Where did Mom take Minho?","options":["To the zoo","To the clinic","To school","To the beach"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"엄마는 민호를 병원(clinic)에 데려갔어요."},{"q":"\"He sneezed twice\" means he sneezed ___.","options":["one time","ten times","never","two times"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"twice는 '두 번'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Minho woke up with a stuffy nose.","She had a small scar on her hand from cooking."],"sents":["Minho woke up with a stuffy nose.","\"Achoo!\" He sneezed twice.","Mom took him to the clinic.","Minho had a little fear of doctors.","But the doctor was quite kind.","She had a small scar on her hand from cooking.","\"Drink warm tea,\" she said.","\"I recommend lots of sleep, too.\""]},{"en":"At home, Minho did not want to bother Mom. She was very busy. Grandma's birthday was tomorrow! \"Let's make a cake,\" said his sister Yuna. They mixed a sweet batter with eggs, milk, and flour. \"Don't stir with too much force,\" Yuna said. \"Do every step in order.\"","ko":"집에서 민호는 엄마를 귀찮게 하고 싶지 않았어요. 엄마는 아주 바빴거든요. 내일은 할머니 생신이었어요! \"케이크를 만들자.\" 누나 유나가 말했어요. 둘은 달걀, 우유, 밀가루로 달콤한 반죽을 섞었어요. \"너무 힘을 세게 줘서 젓지 마.\" 유나가 말했어요. \"모든 단계를 순서대로 해.\"","questions":[{"q":"What did Minho and Yuna make?","options":["A cake batter","A paper hat","A sandwich","Soup"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"둘은 케이크를 만들려고 반죽을 섞었어요."},{"q":"\"Do every step in order\" means do the steps ___.","options":["very fast","with your eyes closed","one after another, the right way","all at once"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"여기서 order는 '순서'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["They mixed a sweet batter with eggs, milk, and flour.","Do every step in order."],"sents":["At home, Minho did not want to bother Mom.","She was very busy.","Grandma's birthday was tomorrow!","\"Let's make a cake,\" said his sister Yuna.","They mixed a sweet batter with eggs, milk, and flour.","\"Don't stir with too much force,\" Yuna said.","\"Do every step in order.\""]},{"en":"While the cake baked, they began to decorate the room. Yuna hung paper flowers. Minho played some classical music. Then he played a reed flute from music class. \"What type of song is that?\" Yuna asked. \"A happy one!\" said Minho. They were careful not to damage the walls.","ko":"케이크가 구워지는 동안, 둘은 방을 꾸미기 시작했어요. 유나는 종이꽃을 달았어요. 민호는 클래식 음악을 틀었어요. 그다음 음악 시간에 쓰는 갈대 피리를 불었어요. \"그건 어떤 종류의 노래야?\" 유나가 물었어요. \"신나는 노래!\" 민호가 말했어요. 둘은 벽이 상하지 않도록 조심했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Yuna hang?","options":["Balloons","Socks","Paper flowers","Pictures"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"유나는 종이꽃을 달았어요."},{"q":"\"Decorate the room\" means ___ the room.","options":["clean","make pretty","leave","lock"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"decorate는 '장식하다, 꾸미다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Minho played some classical music.","They were careful not to damage the walls."],"sents":["While the cake baked, they began to decorate the room.","Yuna hung paper flowers.","Minho played some classical music.","Then he played a reed flute from music class.","\"What type of song is that?\" Yuna asked.","\"A happy one!\" said Minho.","They were careful not to damage the walls."]},{"en":"Then Minho had to review his spelling words. Dad came home and turned on a movie. \"This movie has no violence, so you can watch it too,\" Dad said. The next day, Grandma loved her party. \"I have my own special cake from my grandkids! Such a happy day!\" she said. Minho's nose felt better, too.","ko":"그다음 민호는 받아쓰기 단어를 복습해야 했어요. 아빠가 집에 와서 영화를 틀었어요. \"이 영화에는 폭력이 없으니까 너도 봐도 돼.\" 아빠가 말했어요. 다음 날, 할머니는 파티를 정말 좋아하셨어요. \"손주들이 만든 나만의 특별한 케이크가 있구나! 정말 행복한 날이야!\" 할머니가 말씀하셨어요. 민호의 코도 나아졌어요.","questions":[{"q":"How did Grandma feel about the party?","options":["She was angry","She was sleepy","She was bored","She loved it"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"할머니는 파티를 정말 좋아하셨어요."},{"q":"\"Review his spelling words\" means ___ the words again.","options":["throw away","study","sing","draw"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"review는 '복습하다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Then Minho had to review his spelling words.","Minho's nose felt better, too."],"sents":["Then Minho had to review his spelling words.","Dad came home and turned on a movie.","\"This movie has no violence, so you can watch it too,\" Dad said.","The next day, Grandma loved her party.","\"I have my own special cake from my grandkids!","Such a happy day!\" she said.","Minho's nose felt better, too."]}]},{"key":3,"title":"Sora's Train Museum Trip","ids":["often","painkiller","key","eventful","track","action","beverage","freckle","develop","stomach","argue","advise","mist","surround","appearance","pine","engineer","coal","aware","ability"],"parts":[{"en":"Sora had a freckle on her nose. She often wore a red cap. Today was her school trip to a train museum. Her uncle was an engineer there. In the morning, a soft mist covered the town. Tall pine trees surround the museum. \"Stay together,\" the teacher said. \"Be aware of the train tracks.\"","ko":"소라는 코에 주근깨가 하나 있었어요. 소라는 자주 빨간 모자를 썼어요. 오늘은 기차 박물관으로 가는 학교 소풍 날이었어요. 소라의 삼촌은 그곳의 기술자였어요. 아침에는 엷은 안개가 마을을 덮었어요. 키 큰 소나무들이 박물관을 둘러싸고 있어요. \"함께 다니세요.\" 선생님이 말했어요. \"기차 선로를 조심하세요.\"","questions":[{"q":"Where did Sora's class go?","options":["To a farm","To a train museum","To a pool","To a library"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"소라의 반은 기차 박물관으로 소풍을 갔어요."},{"q":"\"Tall pine trees surround the museum\" means the trees are ___ the museum.","options":["inside","on top of","all around","under"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"surround는 '둘러싸다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Sora had a freckle on her nose.","Her uncle was an engineer there."],"sents":["Sora had a freckle on her nose.","She often wore a red cap.","Today was her school trip to a train museum.","Her uncle was an engineer there.","In the morning, a soft mist covered the town.","Tall pine trees surround the museum.","\"Stay together,\" the teacher said.","\"Be aware of the train tracks.\""]},{"en":"Uncle showed them an old train. \"It used coal to move,\" he said. \"Long ago, people worked hard to develop faster trains.\" Then Sora and her friend Jun began to argue. \"This train is faster!\" \"No, that one is!\" Uncle laughed. \"I advise you both to read the signs.\" They did. They were both wrong!","ko":"삼촌은 아이들에게 오래된 기차를 보여 주었어요. \"이 기차는 석탄으로 움직였어.\" 삼촌이 말했어요. \"옛날에 사람들은 더 빠른 기차를 개발하려고 열심히 일했단다.\" 그때 소라와 친구 준이 말다툼을 시작했어요. \"이 기차가 더 빨라!\" \"아니야, 저게 더 빨라!\" 삼촌이 웃었어요. \"둘 다 표지판을 읽어 보라고 조언할게.\" 둘은 표지판을 읽었어요. 둘 다 틀렸어요!","questions":[{"q":"What did the old train use to move?","options":["Coal","Water","Wind","Batteries"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"삼촌이 그 기차는 석탄으로 움직였다고 했어요."},{"q":"\"Sora and Jun began to argue\" means they began to ___.","options":["sing","sleep","disagree with each other","eat lunch"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"argue는 '말다툼하다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Uncle showed them an old train.","I advise you both to read the signs."],"sents":["Uncle showed them an old train.","\"It used coal to move,\" he said.","\"Long ago, people worked hard to develop faster trains.\" Then Sora and her friend Jun began to argue.","\"This train is faster!\" \"No, that one is!\" Uncle laughed.","\"I advise you both to read the signs.\" They did.","They were both wrong!"]},{"en":"At lunch, Jun's stomach hurt. \"I ate too fast,\" he said. The teacher gave him water, not a painkiller. \"Just rest a little,\" she said. Sora shared her cold beverage. It was apple juice. Soon Jun felt better. \"Thanks, Sora. You have a great ability to help people,\" he said. Sora smiled.","ko":"점심시간에 준은 배가 아팠어요. \"너무 빨리 먹었어.\" 준이 말했어요. 선생님은 진통제가 아니라 물을 주셨어요. \"조금만 쉬렴.\" 선생님이 말했어요. 소라는 시원한 음료를 나눠 주었어요. 사과 주스였어요. 곧 준은 나아졌어요. \"고마워, 소라. 너는 사람들을 돕는 멋진 능력이 있어.\" 준이 말했어요. 소라는 웃었어요.","questions":[{"q":"Why did Jun's stomach hurt?","options":["He ran too much","He ate too fast","He fell down","He was cold"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"준은 너무 빨리 먹어서 배가 아팠어요."},{"q":"A \"beverage\" is ___.","options":["a kind of shoe","a toy train","a sleeping bag","something you drink"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"beverage는 '음료'라는 뜻이에요. 여기서는 사과 주스예요."}],"dictation":["At lunch, Jun's stomach hurt.","Sora shared her cold beverage."],"sents":["At lunch, Jun's stomach hurt.","\"I ate too fast,\" he said.","The teacher gave him water, not a painkiller.","\"Just rest a little,\" she said.","Sora shared her cold beverage.","It was apple juice.","Soon Jun felt better.","\"Thanks, Sora.","You have a great ability to help people,\" he said.","Sora smiled."]},{"en":"Next was the action show. A toy train raced around a small track. Then a man in a train costume made a funny appearance. Everyone clapped! Uncle gave Sora a little gold key. \"It opens a toy train box. It is my gift,\" he said. What an eventful day! Sora wanted to be an engineer too.","ko":"다음은 액션 쇼였어요. 장난감 기차가 작은 트랙을 따라 달렸어요. 그때 기차 옷을 입은 아저씨가 웃기게 등장했어요. 모두 박수를 쳤어요! 삼촌은 소라에게 작은 금색 열쇠를 주었어요. \"이건 장난감 기차 상자를 여는 거야. 내 선물이야.\" 삼촌이 말했어요. 정말 일이 많은 하루였어요! 소라도 기술자가 되고 싶었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Uncle give Sora?","options":["A gold key","A red cap","A train ticket","A cookie"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"삼촌은 소라에게 작은 금색 열쇠를 주었어요."},{"q":"\"An eventful day\" is a day ___.","options":["with nothing to do","with many things happening","that is very short","when you stay in bed"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"eventful은 '다사다난한, 일이 많은'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["A toy train raced around a small track.","Sora wanted to be an engineer too."],"sents":["Next was the action show.","A toy train raced around a small track.","Then a man in a train costume made a funny appearance.","Everyone clapped!","Uncle gave Sora a little gold key.","\"It opens a toy train box.","It is my gift,\" he said.","What an eventful day!","Sora wanted to be an engineer too."]}]},{"key":4,"title":"Yuri and the Striped Kitten","ids":["multiplication","sweep","cultural","opinion","rescue","cycle","frown","head","lightly","trait","striped","allow","shortcut","polish","basic","then","pretend","depend","caution","channel"],"parts":[{"en":"Yuri liked to cycle to school. One morning, she heard a tiny \"meow.\" A striped kitten was stuck in a bush. \"I will rescue you,\" Yuri said. She lightly pulled the branches away. The kitten jumped into her arms. Yuri looked at her watch. \"Oh no! I am late!\" Then she had an idea.","ko":"유리는 자전거를 타고 학교에 가는 것을 좋아했어요. 어느 날 아침, 작은 \"야옹\" 소리가 들렸어요. 줄무늬 새끼 고양이가 덤불에 갇혀 있었어요. \"내가 구해 줄게.\" 유리가 말했어요. 유리는 나뭇가지를 살짝 치웠어요. 새끼 고양이가 유리 품으로 뛰어들었어요. 유리는 시계를 보았어요. \"아, 안 돼! 늦었어!\" 그때 유리에게 좋은 생각이 떠올랐어요.","questions":[{"q":"Where was the kitten stuck?","options":["In a tree","In a box","In a bush","On a roof"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"줄무늬 새끼 고양이는 덤불에 갇혀 있었어요."},{"q":"\"I will rescue you\" means I will ___ you.","options":["save","chase","draw","feed"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"rescue는 '구조하다, 구하다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Yuri liked to cycle to school.","A striped kitten was stuck in a bush."],"sents":["Yuri liked to cycle to school.","One morning, she heard a tiny \"meow.\" A striped kitten was stuck in a bush.","\"I will rescue you,\" Yuri said.","She lightly pulled the branches away.","The kitten jumped into her arms.","Yuri looked at her watch.","\"Oh no!","I am late!\" Then she had an idea."]},{"en":"She took a shortcut through the park. A sign said, \"Caution! Wet path.\" So Yuri rode slowly. At school, her teacher began to frown. \"Yuri, you are late.\" Yuri showed her the kitten. The teacher smiled. \"Okay. I will allow the kitten to stay in a box today. Now, let's do basic multiplication.\"","ko":"유리는 공원을 지나는 지름길로 갔어요. 표지판에 \"주의! 길이 젖어 있음.\"이라고 쓰여 있었어요. 그래서 유리는 천천히 달렸어요. 학교에서 선생님이 얼굴을 찡그리기 시작했어요. \"유리야, 늦었구나.\" 유리는 선생님께 새끼 고양이를 보여 드렸어요. 선생님이 웃으셨어요. \"좋아. 오늘은 고양이가 상자 안에 있도록 허락할게. 이제 기초 곱셈을 해 보자.\"","questions":[{"q":"Why did Yuri ride slowly?","options":["She was tired","The path was wet","Her bike was broken","She was sad"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"표지판에 길이 젖어 있다고 쓰여 있어서 천천히 달렸어요."},{"q":"A \"shortcut\" is a way that is ___.","options":["longer","closed","faster or shorter","very dark"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"shortcut은 '지름길'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["She took a shortcut through the park.","At school, her teacher began to frown."],"sents":["She took a shortcut through the park.","A sign said, \"Caution!","Wet path.\" So Yuri rode slowly.","At school, her teacher began to frown.","\"Yuri, you are late.\" Yuri showed her the kitten.","The teacher smiled.","\"Okay.","I will allow the kitten to stay in a box today.","Now, let's do basic multiplication.\""]},{"en":"The kitten slept while the class did math. Two times three is six! After that, the class had a cultural show. Kids wore hanbok, kimonos, and more. Then Yuri had to sweep the floor. The kitten wanted to help. It liked to pretend the broom was a toy. Everyone laughed.","ko":"반 친구들이 수학을 하는 동안 새끼 고양이는 잠을 잤어요. 2 곱하기 3은 6이에요! 그다음 반에서 문화 공연을 했어요. 아이들은 한복, 기모노 등을 입었어요. 그 후 유리는 바닥을 쓸어야 했어요. 새끼 고양이도 돕고 싶었어요. 고양이는 빗자루가 장난감인 척하기를 좋아했어요. 모두 웃었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Yuri have to do after the show?","options":["Sweep the floor","Sing a song","Go home","Wash the kitten"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"공연이 끝난 후 유리는 바닥을 쓸어야 했어요."},{"q":"\"It liked to pretend the broom was a toy\" means the kitten ___.","options":["broke the broom","acted like the broom was a toy","hid the broom","was afraid of the broom"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"pretend는 '~인 척하다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["The kitten slept while the class did math.","Then Yuri had to sweep the floor."],"sents":["The kitten slept while the class did math.","Two times three is six!","After that, the class had a cultural show.","Kids wore hanbok, kimonos, and more.","Then Yuri had to sweep the floor.","The kitten wanted to help.","It liked to pretend the broom was a toy.","Everyone laughed."]},{"en":"After school, Yuri asked her friends, \"What is your opinion? Can I keep the kitten?\" \"It will depend on your mom,\" said Jisu. At home, Mom was watching an animal channel. She saw the kitten and smiled. \"Being kind is your best trait,\" Mom said. Then Yuri helped Dad polish her bike. Finally, they all headed inside.","ko":"방과 후에 유리는 친구들에게 물었어요. \"너희 의견은 어때? 내가 고양이를 키워도 될까?\" \"그건 너희 엄마에게 달려 있어.\" 지수가 말했어요. 집에서 엄마는 동물 채널을 보고 있었어요. 엄마는 새끼 고양이를 보고 웃었어요. \"친절한 것이 너의 가장 좋은 특징이야.\" 엄마가 말했어요. 그다음 유리는 아빠를 도와 자전거를 닦았어요. 마침내 모두 집 안으로 향했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What was Mom watching?","options":["A cooking show","A soccer game","A movie","An animal channel"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"엄마는 동물 채널을 보고 있었어요."},{"q":"\"Polish her bike\" means ___ her bike.","options":["sell","ride","rub and clean","paint"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"polish는 '닦다, 윤을 내다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["At home, Mom was watching an animal channel.","Then Yuri helped Dad polish her bike."],"sents":["After school, Yuri asked her friends, \"What is your opinion?","Can I keep the kitten?\" \"It will depend on your mom,\" said Jisu.","At home, Mom was watching an animal channel.","She saw the kitten and smiled.","\"Being kind is your best trait,\" Mom said.","Then Yuri helped Dad polish her bike.","Finally, they all headed inside."]}]},{"key":5,"title":"Princess Eunji's Big Play","ids":["line","rob","disabled","beauty","even","raisin","setting","ladder","anymore","microwave","confidence","nephew","language","stink","appointment","sniff","ancient","theater","loyal","frill"],"parts":[{"en":"Eunji's class was making a play. The setting was an ancient castle. Eunji was the princess. Her dress had a pink frill. The kids stood in a line on the stage. Eunji felt nervous. \"I am scared,\" she said. At home, her loyal dog, Bori, licked her hand. Bori wanted to give her confidence.","ko":"은지네 반은 연극을 만들고 있었어요. 배경은 아주 오래된 성이었어요. 은지는 공주였어요. 은지의 드레스에는 분홍색 프릴이 있었어요. 아이들은 무대 위에 한 줄로 섰어요. 은지는 긴장했어요. \"무서워.\" 은지가 말했어요. 집에서 은지의 충실한 강아지 보리가 은지의 손을 핥았어요. 보리는 은지에게 자신감을 주고 싶었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What was Eunji in the play?","options":["A fox","The princess","A king","A dog"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"은지는 연극에서 공주였어요."},{"q":"\"The setting was an ancient castle\" means the castle was ___.","options":["very old","very small","made of candy","brand new"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"ancient는 '고대의, 아주 오래된'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["The setting was an ancient castle.","Her dress had a pink frill."],"sents":["Eunji's class was making a play.","The setting was an ancient castle.","Eunji was the princess.","Her dress had a pink frill.","The kids stood in a line on the stage.","Eunji felt nervous.","\"I am scared,\" she said.","At home, her loyal dog, Bori, licked her hand.","Bori wanted to give her confidence."]},{"en":"Eunji's aunt came to visit with her nephew, Tae. Tae was disabled and used a wheelchair. He loved stories. \"Can I help you practice?\" he asked. Tae read all the parts in funny voices. He even said one part in Spanish! \"I love learning a new language,\" Tae said. Eunji laughed and felt better.","ko":"은지의 이모가 조카 태와 함께 놀러 왔어요. 태는 장애가 있어서 휠체어를 탔어요. 태는 이야기를 좋아했어요. \"연습하는 거 도와줄까?\" 태가 물었어요. 태는 모든 역할을 웃긴 목소리로 읽었어요. 태는 한 부분을 스페인어로 말하기까지 했어요! \"나는 새로운 언어를 배우는 게 좋아.\" 태가 말했어요. 은지는 웃었고 기분이 나아졌어요.","questions":[{"q":"How did Tae help Eunji?","options":["He made her dress","He drove her to school","He helped her practice","He fed Bori"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"태는 웃긴 목소리로 역할을 읽으며 연습을 도와주었어요."},{"q":"A \"language\" is ___.","options":["a kind of food","a way people talk, like English","a musical instrument","a game"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"language는 '언어, 말'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Tae was disabled and used a wheelchair.","He even said one part in Spanish!"],"sents":["Eunji's aunt came to visit with her nephew, Tae.","Tae was disabled and used a wheelchair.","He loved stories.","\"Can I help you practice?\" he asked.","Tae read all the parts in funny voices.","He even said one part in Spanish!","\"I love learning a new language,\" Tae said.","Eunji laughed and felt better."]},{"en":"Then they made a snack. Tae put popcorn in the microwave. Soon it began to stink! Eunji gave a sniff. \"Oh no, it's burning!\" They opened the windows. \"Let's eat raisin cookies instead,\" said Aunt. They talked about the play again. In the story, a sneaky fox tries to rob the castle. Tae made a great fox!","ko":"그다음 그들은 간식을 만들었어요. 태가 팝콘을 전자레인지에 넣었어요. 곧 고약한 냄새가 나기 시작했어요! 은지는 코를 킁킁거렸어요. \"아, 안 돼, 타고 있어!\" 그들은 창문을 열었어요. \"대신 건포도 쿠키를 먹자.\" 이모가 말했어요. 그들은 다시 연극 이야기를 했어요. 이야기 속에서 교활한 여우가 성을 털려고 해요. 태는 멋진 여우 역할을 했어요!","questions":[{"q":"What happened to the popcorn?","options":["It burned","It was delicious","It fell on the floor","Bori ate it"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"팝콘이 타면서 고약한 냄새가 났어요."},{"q":"\"It began to stink\" means it began to ___.","options":["smell bad","taste sweet","make music","get cold"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"stink는 '악취가 나다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Tae put popcorn in the microwave.","Soon it began to stink!"],"sents":["Then they made a snack.","Tae put popcorn in the microwave.","Soon it began to stink!","Eunji gave a sniff.","\"Oh no, it's burning!\" They opened the windows.","\"Let's eat raisin cookies instead,\" said Aunt.","They talked about the play again.","In the story, a sneaky fox tries to rob the castle.","Tae made a great fox!"]},{"en":"On Friday, Eunji had an appointment at the theater for the show. A man climbed a ladder to fix the lights. Then the play began. Eunji was not scared anymore. She said every word clearly. Everyone talked about the beauty of the castle. Tae clapped the loudest. \"You were wonderful!\" he said.","ko":"금요일에 은지는 공연을 위해 극장에 가기로 약속이 있었어요. 한 아저씨가 사다리를 타고 올라가 조명을 고쳤어요. 그리고 연극이 시작되었어요. 은지는 더 이상 무섭지 않았어요. 은지는 모든 말을 또박또박 했어요. 모두 성의 아름다움에 대해 이야기했어요. 태가 가장 크게 박수를 쳤어요. \"너 정말 멋졌어!\" 태가 말했어요.","questions":[{"q":"Who clapped the loudest?","options":["Bori","The man on the ladder","Aunt","Tae"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"태가 가장 크게 박수를 쳤어요."},{"q":"\"Eunji was not scared anymore\" means ___.","options":["she was still scared","she stopped being scared","she was scared at home","she was always scared"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"not ~ anymore는 '더 이상 ~않다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["A man climbed a ladder to fix the lights.","Eunji was not scared anymore."],"sents":["On Friday, Eunji had an appointment at the theater for the show.","A man climbed a ladder to fix the lights.","Then the play began.","Eunji was not scared anymore.","She said every word clearly.","Everyone talked about the beauty of the castle.","Tae clapped the loudest.","\"You were wonderful!\" he said."]}]},{"key":6,"title":"Dohyun the Fossil Hunter","ids":["monthly","fossil","prepare","select","demand","pan","anybody","polite","produce","flash","documentary","misunderstand","likely","tornado","juicy","smash","safety","design","slip","broad"],"parts":[{"en":"Dohyun loved dinosaurs. He read a monthly science magazine. One day, he watched a documentary about a fossil hunter. \"I want to find a fossil too!\" he said. Mom smiled. \"Then let's prepare for a trip to the dig site.\" Dohyun packed a hat, a water bottle, and a small brush.","ko":"도현이는 공룡을 좋아했어요. 도현이는 월간 과학 잡지를 읽었어요. 어느 날, 도현이는 화석 탐험가에 대한 다큐멘터리를 보았어요. \"나도 화석을 찾고 싶어!\" 도현이가 말했어요. 엄마가 웃었어요. \"그럼 발굴 현장으로 갈 여행을 준비하자.\" 도현이는 모자, 물병, 작은 붓을 챙겼어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Dohyun pack?","options":["A hat, a water bottle, and a brush","A ball and a bat","A pillow and a blanket","A cake"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"도현이는 모자, 물병, 작은 붓을 챙겼어요."},{"q":"\"Let's prepare for a trip\" means let's ___ the trip.","options":["cancel","forget","get ready for","draw"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"prepare는 '준비하다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["He read a monthly science magazine.","Dohyun packed a hat, a water bottle, and a small brush."],"sents":["Dohyun loved dinosaurs.","He read a monthly science magazine.","One day, he watched a documentary about a fossil hunter.","\"I want to find a fossil too!\" he said.","Mom smiled.","\"Then let's prepare for a trip to the dig site.\" Dohyun packed a hat, a water bottle, and a small brush."]},{"en":"At the dig site, there was a broad, sandy field. A guide talked about safety. \"Wear gloves and do not run,\" she said. \"You may slip on the rocks.\" Dohyun had to select a spot. He chose one near a big rock. He brushed the sand very slowly. Then he saw a flash of white!","ko":"발굴 현장에는 넓은 모래 들판이 있었어요. 안내원이 안전에 대해 이야기했어요. \"장갑을 끼고 뛰지 마세요.\" 안내원이 말했어요. \"바위에서 미끄러질 수 있어요.\" 도현이는 장소를 하나 골라야 했어요. 도현이는 큰 바위 근처를 골랐어요. 도현이는 모래를 아주 천천히 쓸어냈어요. 그때 하얀 것이 번쩍하는 게 보였어요!","questions":[{"q":"What did the guide talk about?","options":["Lunch","Safety","Dinosaur songs","Homework"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"안내원은 안전에 대해 이야기했어요."},{"q":"\"Dohyun had to select a spot\" means he had to ___ a spot.","options":["choose","clean","leave","hide"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"select는 '선택하다, 고르다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["At the dig site, there was a broad, sandy field.","He brushed the sand very slowly."],"sents":["At the dig site, there was a broad, sandy field.","A guide talked about safety.","\"Wear gloves and do not run,\" she said.","\"You may slip on the rocks.\" Dohyun had to select a spot.","He chose one near a big rock.","He brushed the sand very slowly.","Then he saw a flash of white!"]},{"en":"It was a tiny shell fossil! \"Does anybody have a bag?\" Dohyun asked. A girl gave him one. \"Thank you,\" he said. Dohyun was always polite. The girl had a dinosaur design on her shirt. \"Be careful. Don't smash it,\" she said. \"I won't,\" said Dohyun. \"It is likely very, very old.\"","ko":"그것은 작은 조개 화석이었어요! \"누구 봉지 있는 사람 있어요?\" 도현이가 물었어요. 한 여자아이가 봉지를 주었어요. \"고마워.\" 도현이가 말했어요. 도현이는 항상 예의 발랐어요. 그 아이의 셔츠에는 공룡 무늬가 있었어요. \"조심해. 부수지 마.\" 그 아이가 말했어요. \"안 그럴게.\" 도현이가 말했어요. \"아마 아주아주 오래된 것 같아.\"","questions":[{"q":"What did Dohyun find?","options":["A gold coin","A dinosaur egg","A tiny shell fossil","A toy car"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"도현이는 작은 조개 화석을 찾았어요."},{"q":"\"Dohyun was always polite\" means he always ___.","options":["ran fast","talked loudly","slept late","used kind manners"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"polite는 '예의 바른, 공손한'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Does anybody have a bag?","The girl had a dinosaur design on her shirt."],"sents":["It was a tiny shell fossil!","\"Does anybody have a bag?\" Dohyun asked.","A girl gave him one.","\"Thank you,\" he said.","Dohyun was always polite.","The girl had a dinosaur design on her shirt.","\"Be careful.","Don't smash it,\" she said.","\"I won't,\" said Dohyun.","\"It is likely very, very old.\""]},{"en":"For lunch, a farm truck sold fresh produce. Dohyun ate a juicy peach. Mom cooked eggs in a small pan. The radio said a tornado was far away in another country. \"Don't misunderstand. We are safe here,\" Mom said. Back home, his little brother began to demand, \"Show me the fossil!\" Dohyun proudly showed him.","ko":"점심으로 농장 트럭이 신선한 농산물을 팔았어요. 도현이는 즙이 많은 복숭아를 먹었어요. 엄마는 작은 프라이팬에 달걀을 요리했어요. 라디오에서 토네이도가 아주 먼 다른 나라에 있다고 했어요. \"오해하지 마. 우리는 여기서 안전해.\" 엄마가 말했어요. 집에 돌아오자 남동생이 \"화석 보여 줘!\" 하고 조르기 시작했어요. 도현이는 자랑스럽게 화석을 보여 주었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Dohyun eat for lunch?","options":["A juicy peach","A hamburger","Pizza","Ice cream"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"도현이는 즙이 많은 복숭아를 먹었어요."},{"q":"\"Fresh produce\" means fresh ___.","options":["toys","fruits and vegetables from a farm","clothes","books"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"produce는 '농산물'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Dohyun ate a juicy peach.","Mom cooked eggs in a small pan."],"sents":["For lunch, a farm truck sold fresh produce.","Dohyun ate a juicy peach.","Mom cooked eggs in a small pan.","The radio said a tornado was far away in another country.","\"Don't misunderstand.","We are safe here,\" Mom said.","Back home, his little brother began to demand, \"Show me the fossil!\" Dohyun proudly showed him."]}]},{"key":7,"title":"A Song for Baby Park","ids":["sample","dead","rainfall","joyful","yet","lyric","propose","neighbor","annoy","frequent","muscle","birth","adventure","understand","also","rhyme","fat","copy","habitat","double"],"parts":[{"en":"Jieun's neighbor, Mrs. Park, had a new baby. The birth was last week. \"Let's write a song for the baby!\" Jieun said to her brother Hojun. \"Okay, but I can't write songs yet,\" said Hojun. \"That's fine. We can learn together,\" said Jieun. It was a joyful idea, and they started right away.","ko":"지은이의 이웃인 박 아주머니가 아기를 낳았어요. 아기는 지난주에 태어났어요. \"아기를 위한 노래를 만들자!\" 지은이가 남동생 호준이에게 말했어요. \"좋아, 그런데 나는 아직 노래를 못 만들어.\" 호준이가 말했어요. \"괜찮아. 같이 배우면 돼.\" 지은이가 말했어요. 그것은 즐거운 생각이었고, 둘은 바로 시작했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Jieun want to write?","options":["A letter","A song for the baby","A storybook","A shopping list"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"지은이는 아기를 위한 노래를 만들고 싶었어요."},{"q":"\"I can't write songs yet\" means Hojun ___.","options":["will never write songs","hates songs","can't write songs now, but maybe later","writes songs every day"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"yet은 '아직'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["The birth was last week.","It was a joyful idea, and they started right away."],"sents":["Jieun's neighbor, Mrs.","Park, had a new baby.","The birth was last week.","\"Let's write a song for the baby!\" Jieun said to her brother Hojun.","\"Okay, but I can't write songs yet,\" said Hojun.","\"That's fine.","We can learn together,\" said Jieun.","It was a joyful idea, and they started right away."]},{"en":"First, they needed a lyric. \"Baby, baby, sweet and small,\" Jieun sang. \"You are the cutest one of all!\" \"Hey, small and all rhyme!\" said Hojun. He tried to copy her singing. Then Jieun's tablet stopped. The battery in the tablet was dead. \"Oh no!\" They also needed a guitar.","ko":"먼저 둘은 가사가 필요했어요. \"아기야, 아기야, 귀엽고 작은 아기야.\" 지은이가 노래했어요. \"너는 세상에서 제일 귀여워!\" \"와, small이랑 all이 운이 맞아!\" 호준이가 말했어요. 호준이는 누나의 노래를 따라 하려고 했어요. 그때 지은이의 태블릿이 꺼졌어요. 배터리가 다 됐어요. \"아, 안 돼!\" 둘은 기타도 필요했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What happened to Jieun's tablet?","options":["The battery was dead","It fell in water","Hojun broke it","It played a song"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"태블릿의 배터리가 다 되어서 꺼졌어요."},{"q":"\"He tried to copy her singing\" means he tried to ___.","options":["stop her singing","sing the same way she did","write her name","laugh at her"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"copy는 '베끼다, 따라 하다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["The battery in the tablet was dead.","They also needed a guitar."],"sents":["First, they needed a lyric.","\"Baby, baby, sweet and small,\" Jieun sang.","\"You are the cutest one of all!\" \"Hey, small and all rhyme!\" said Hojun.","He tried to copy her singing.","Then Jieun's tablet stopped.","The battery in the tablet was dead.","\"Oh no!\" They also needed a guitar."]},{"en":"So they went to Grandpa's house. Rainfall was frequent that month, so they took umbrellas. Grandpa had a fat orange cat named Toto. Toto liked to annoy Hojun by sitting on his paper. Grandpa lent them his guitar. \"Play a sample song first,\" Hojun said. Grandpa played and showed off his arm muscle. Everyone laughed.","ko":"그래서 둘은 할아버지 댁에 갔어요. 그달에는 비가 자주 와서 우산을 챙겼어요. 할아버지에게는 토토라는 뚱뚱한 주황색 고양이가 있었어요. 토토는 호준이의 종이 위에 앉아서 호준이를 짜증나게 하는 걸 좋아했어요. 할아버지는 기타를 빌려주셨어요. \"먼저 샘플 노래를 연주해 주세요.\" 호준이가 말했어요. 할아버지는 연주하면서 팔 근육을 자랑하셨어요. 모두 웃었어요.","questions":[{"q":"Why did they take umbrellas?","options":["It was very sunny","It was snowing","Grandpa asked them to","It rained often that month"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"그달에는 비가 자주 와서 우산을 챙겼어요."},{"q":"\"Rainfall was frequent\" means it rained ___.","options":["often","never","only once","very quietly"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"frequent는 '잦은, 빈번한'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Grandpa had a fat orange cat named Toto.","Grandpa lent them his guitar."],"sents":["So they went to Grandpa's house.","Rainfall was frequent that month, so they took umbrellas.","Grandpa had a fat orange cat named Toto.","Toto liked to annoy Hojun by sitting on his paper.","Grandpa lent them his guitar.","\"Play a sample song first,\" Hojun said.","Grandpa played and showed off his arm muscle.","Everyone laughed."]},{"en":"Then Jieun had a plan. \"I propose a double guitar part,\" she said. Grandpa helped them practice. On Sunday, they sang for Mrs. Park. The baby smiled. \"Our street is the baby's happy habitat,\" Grandpa joked. \"Now I understand. Making songs is an adventure!\" said Hojun. Mrs. Park gave them big hugs.","ko":"그때 지은이에게 계획이 생겼어요. \"기타 파트를 두 배로 하자고 제안할게.\" 지은이가 말했어요. 할아버지는 연습을 도와주셨어요. 일요일에 그들은 박 아주머니를 위해 노래를 불렀어요. 아기가 웃었어요. \"우리 동네가 아기의 행복한 서식지구나.\" 할아버지가 농담을 하셨어요. \"이제 알겠어. 노래 만들기는 모험이야!\" 호준이가 말했어요. 박 아주머니는 그들을 꼭 안아 주었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did the baby do when they sang?","options":["Cried","Slept","Smiled","Ran away"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"노래를 부르자 아기가 웃었어요."},{"q":"\"I propose a double guitar part\" means Jieun ___ a double guitar part.","options":["suggests","breaks","hides","sells"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"propose는 '제안하다'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["On Sunday, they sang for Mrs. Park.","Mrs. Park gave them big hugs."],"sents":["Then Jieun had a plan.","\"I propose a double guitar part,\" she said.","Grandpa helped them practice.","On Sunday, they sang for Mrs.","Park.","The baby smiled.","\"Our street is the baby's happy habitat,\" Grandpa joked.","\"Now I understand.","Making songs is an adventure!\" said Hojun.","Mrs.","Park gave them big hugs."]}]},{"key":8,"title":"Arin and the Archer Note","ids":["exist","brand","archer","honest","medium","length","marriage","spelling","wage","appear","control","tough","difference","period","unknown","note","pleased","architect","battle","suck"],"parts":[{"en":"Arin's grandparents had a long marriage. It was fifty years! Arin wanted to make them a gift. Her mom was an architect. \"Let's build a little house from paper,\" Mom said. Arin measured the length of each wall. \"Medium walls, not too tall,\" she said. It was tough work, but it was fun.","ko":"아린이의 할머니 할아버지는 오랫동안 결혼 생활을 하셨어요. 50년이나요! 아린이는 두 분께 선물을 만들어 드리고 싶었어요. 아린이의 엄마는 건축가였어요. \"종이로 작은 집을 만들자.\" 엄마가 말했어요. 아린이는 벽마다 길이를 쟀어요. \"중간 크기의 벽, 너무 높지 않게.\" 아린이가 말했어요. 힘든 일이었지만 재미있었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What was Arin's mom's job?","options":["A doctor","A teacher","An architect","A cook"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"아린이의 엄마는 건축가였어요."},{"q":"\"It was tough work\" means the work was ___.","options":["hard","easy","boring","quick"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"tough는 '힘든, 어려운'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Arin's grandparents had a long marriage.","Arin measured the length of each wall."],"sents":["Arin's grandparents had a long marriage.","It was fifty years!","Arin wanted to make them a gift.","Her mom was an architect.","\"Let's build a little house from paper,\" Mom said.","Arin measured the length of each wall.","\"Medium walls, not too tall,\" she said.","It was tough work, but it was fun."]},{"en":"Then Arin found a note in Grandpa's old book. It said, \"Find the archer.\" \"Who is the archer?\" Arin asked. It was an unknown puzzle! Arin tried to control her excitement. She used a straw to suck up her juice and think. \"Does a real archer exist in our family?\" she wondered.","ko":"그때 아린이는 할아버지의 오래된 책에서 쪽지를 발견했어요. 쪽지에는 \"궁수를 찾아라.\"라고 쓰여 있었어요. \"궁수가 누구지?\" 아린이가 물었어요. 그것은 알려지지 않은 수수께끼였어요! 아린이는 신나는 마음을 진정시키려고 했어요. 아린이는 빨대로 주스를 빨아 마시며 생각했어요. \"우리 가족 중에 진짜 궁수가 있을까?\" 아린이는 궁금했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did the note say?","options":["Find the cat","Find the archer","Find the cake","Go to bed"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"쪽지에는 '궁수를 찾아라'라고 쓰여 있었어요."},{"q":"\"It was an unknown puzzle\" means ___.","options":["everyone knew the answer","it was very easy","it was a jigsaw puzzle","nobody knew the answer yet"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"unknown은 '알려지지 않은'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Then Arin found a note in Grandpa's old book.","She used a straw to suck up her juice and think."],"sents":["Then Arin found a note in Grandpa's old book.","It said, \"Find the archer.\" \"Who is the archer?\" Arin asked.","It was an unknown puzzle!","Arin tried to control her excitement.","She used a straw to suck up her juice and think.","\"Does a real archer exist in our family?\" she wondered."]},{"en":"Arin asked Grandma. Grandma laughed. \"Grandpa was an archer at school! He won a friendly battle at the school fair. Later, he got his first job. His wage was very small. But he bought me a red ribbon with it.\" \"That is so sweet,\" said Arin. \"I am being honest. I love this story!\"","ko":"아린이는 할머니께 여쭈어 보았어요. 할머니가 웃으셨어요. \"할아버지는 학교에서 궁수였단다! 학교 축제에서 친선 시합에서 이겼지. 나중에 할아버지는 첫 직장을 얻었어. 월급은 아주 적었단다. 하지만 그 돈으로 나에게 빨간 리본을 사 줬지.\" \"정말 다정해요.\" 아린이가 말했어요. \"솔직히 말할게요. 이 이야기가 정말 좋아요!\"","questions":[{"q":"What did Grandpa buy Grandma?","options":["A red ribbon","A bow and arrow","A paper house","A book"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"할아버지는 첫 월급으로 빨간 리본을 사 주셨어요."},{"q":"\"His wage was very small\" means ___ was small.","options":["his hat","the money he got for working","his school","his house"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"wage는 '임금, 급료'라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Grandpa was an archer at school!","His wage was very small."],"sents":["Arin asked Grandma.","Grandma laughed.","\"Grandpa was an archer at school!","He won a friendly battle at the school fair.","Later, he got his first job.","His wage was very small.","But he bought me a red ribbon with it.\" \"That is so sweet,\" said Arin.","\"I am being honest.","I love this story!\""]},{"en":"Arin wrote a card for the paper house. She checked her spelling twice. She put a period at the end of each sentence. She drew a tiny archer with her favorite brand of pencils. Big smiles began to appear on her grandparents' faces. Grandpa was very pleased. \"I see no difference between this gift and a treasure!\" he said.","ko":"아린이는 종이집에 넣을 카드를 썼어요. 아린이는 맞춤법을 두 번 확인했어요. 문장마다 끝에 마침표를 찍었어요. 가장 좋아하는 브랜드의 색연필로 작은 궁수를 그렸어요. 할머니 할아버지의 얼굴에 함박웃음이 나타나기 시작했어요. 할아버지는 아주 기뻐하셨어요. \"이 선물과 보물은 전혀 다르지 않구나!\" 할아버지가 말씀하셨어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Arin draw on the card?","options":["A red car","A big cake","A cat","A tiny archer"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"아린이는 카드에 작은 궁수를 그렸어요."},{"q":"\"Grandpa was very pleased\" means Grandpa was very ___.","options":["angry","happy","sleepy","hungry"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"pleased는 '기쁜, 만족한'이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["She checked her spelling twice.","She put a period at the end of each sentence."],"sents":["Arin wrote a card for the paper house.","She checked her spelling twice.","She put a period at the end of each sentence.","She drew a tiny archer with her favorite brand of pencils.","Big smiles began to appear on her grandparents' faces.","Grandpa was very pleased.","\"I see no difference between this gift and a treasure!\" he said."]}]},{"key":9,"title":"Minji's Smile Cake","ids":["shortly","fright","core","afterward","scene","program","couple","moment","puzzled","equal","careless","cheerful","solution","pat","nobody","moist","bold","bare","lid","passionate"],"parts":[{"en":"Minji was a cheerful girl who loved to bake. She was passionate about cakes. One day, her favorite TV program asked kids to send in a cake recipe. \"I will make an apple cake!\" Minji said. She took a couple of red apples from the kitchen. She cut out the core of each apple. Shortly after, the kitchen smelled sweet.","ko":"민지는 빵 굽기를 좋아하는 명랑한 소녀였어요. 민지는 케이크에 열정적이었어요. 어느 날, 민지가 가장 좋아하는 TV 프로그램에서 아이들에게 케이크 레시피를 보내 달라고 했어요. \"사과 케이크를 만들 거야!\" 민지가 말했어요. 민지는 부엌에서 빨간 사과 두어 개를 꺼냈어요. 사과마다 속심을 잘라 냈어요. 얼마 안 되어 부엌에서 달콤한 냄새가 났어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Minji decide to make?","options":["A pizza","An apple cake","Cookies","A sandwich"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"민지는 \"I will make an apple cake!\"라고 말했어요."},{"q":"In the story, what is the \"core\" of an apple?","options":["The red skin","The leaf","The middle part with seeds","The juice"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"core는 과일의 속, 심을 뜻해요. 씨가 있는 가운데 부분이에요."}],"dictation":["She was passionate about cakes.","She cut out the core of each apple."],"sents":["Minji was a cheerful girl who loved to bake.","She was passionate about cakes.","One day, her favorite TV program asked kids to send in a cake recipe.","\"I will make an apple cake!\" Minji said.","She took a couple of red apples from the kitchen.","She cut out the core of each apple.","Shortly after, the kitchen smelled sweet."]},{"en":"She mixed flour and sugar in equal amounts. Then she put the cake in the oven. Her little brother Jun ran in. He was careless and bumped the table. The lid of the sugar jar fell. Crash! For a moment, everyone froze in fright. Luckily, the cake was safe. It came out soft and moist.","ko":"민지는 밀가루와 설탕을 같은 양으로 섞었어요. 그런 다음 케이크를 오븐에 넣었어요. 남동생 준이 뛰어 들어왔어요. 준은 조심성이 없어서 식탁에 부딪혔어요. 설탕 통 뚜껑이 떨어졌어요. 쨍그랑! 잠깐 동안 모두 놀라서 얼어붙었어요. 다행히 케이크는 무사했어요. 케이크는 부드럽고 촉촉하게 구워졌어요.","questions":[{"q":"What fell off the table?","options":["The cake","The lid of the sugar jar","An apple","A spoon"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"\"The lid of the sugar jar fell.\" 설탕 통 뚜껑이 떨어졌어요."},{"q":"The cake was \"moist.\" What does \"moist\" mean here?","options":["Burnt","Hard and dry","Very cold","Soft and a little wet"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"moist는 촉촉한이라는 뜻이에요. 케이크가 촉촉하게 잘 구워졌어요."}],"dictation":["She mixed flour and sugar in equal amounts.","He was careless and bumped the table."],"sents":["She mixed flour and sugar in equal amounts.","Then she put the cake in the oven.","Her little brother Jun ran in.","He was careless and bumped the table.","The lid of the sugar jar fell.","Crash!","For a moment, everyone froze in fright.","Luckily, the cake was safe.","It came out soft and moist."]},{"en":"But the top of the cake looked bare. \"It needs something,\" Minji said. She looked puzzled. Jun had an idea. \"Let's draw a smile with chocolate!\" That was a good solution. Minji wrote SMILE in big, bold letters. Nobody in the family could stop smiling. Even Dad laughed out loud.","ko":"하지만 케이크 윗부분이 텅 비어 보였어요. \"뭔가 필요해.\" 민지가 말했어요. 민지는 어리둥절한 표정이었어요. 준에게 좋은 생각이 떠올랐어요. \"초콜릿으로 웃는 얼굴을 그리자!\" 그건 좋은 해결책이었어요. 민지는 크고 굵은 글씨로 SMILE이라고 썼어요. 가족 중 아무도 웃음을 멈출 수 없었어요. 아빠도 소리 내어 웃었어요.","questions":[{"q":"Whose idea was it to draw with chocolate?","options":["Jun's","Mom's","Dad's","Minji's friend's"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"준이 \"Let's draw a smile with chocolate!\"라고 제안했어요."},{"q":"The top of the cake looked \"bare.\" What does \"bare\" mean here?","options":["Very sweet","Empty, with nothing on it","Broken","Too big"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"bare는 텅 빈이라는 뜻이에요. 케이크 위에 아무 장식이 없었어요."}],"dictation":["But the top of the cake looked bare.","Nobody in the family could stop smiling."],"sents":["But the top of the cake looked bare.","\"It needs something,\" Minji said.","She looked puzzled.","Jun had an idea.","\"Let's draw a smile with chocolate!\" That was a good solution.","Minji wrote SMILE in big, bold letters.","Nobody in the family could stop smiling.","Even Dad laughed out loud."]},{"en":"Minji took a photo of the cake. She sent it to the TV program. A week afterward, a letter came. Minji's cake would be on TV! On the show, there was a funny scene. Jun licked chocolate from his fingers. Mom gave Minji a pat on the head. \"You did a great job,\" she said. Minji felt so proud.","ko":"민지는 케이크 사진을 찍었어요. 그리고 그 사진을 TV 프로그램에 보냈어요. 일주일 후에 편지가 왔어요. 민지의 케이크가 TV에 나오게 된 거예요! 방송에는 재미있는 장면이 있었어요. 준이 손가락에 묻은 초콜릿을 핥아 먹었거든요. 엄마는 민지의 머리를 토닥여 주었어요. \"정말 잘했어.\" 엄마가 말했어요. 민지는 무척 자랑스러웠어요.","questions":[{"q":"What came a week later?","options":["A new oven","A box of apples","A letter","A cake"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"A week afterward, a letter came.\" 일주일 후에 편지가 왔어요."},{"q":"Mom gave Minji a \"pat\" on the head. What is a pat?","options":["A gentle touch with the hand","A big hat","A loud shout","A kiss on the cheek"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"pat은 손으로 가볍게 토닥거리는 것을 뜻해요."}],"dictation":["She sent it to the TV program.","On the show, there was a funny scene."],"sents":["Minji took a photo of the cake.","She sent it to the TV program.","A week afterward, a letter came.","Minji's cake would be on TV!","On the show, there was a funny scene.","Jun licked chocolate from his fingers.","Mom gave Minji a pat on the head.","\"You did a great job,\" she said.","Minji felt so proud."]}]},{"key":10,"title":"Hana and Grandpa's Secret Box","ids":["stick","joy","league","germ","object","explorer","smoke","extra","portrait","brilliant","meaningful","hump","seem","northern","anger","deaf","present","face","farmland","anyway"],"parts":[{"en":"Hana wanted to be an explorer. In summer, she visited Grandpa in a northern town. His house was next to wide farmland. Hana took a long stick and walked across the fields. She saw smoke from a chimney far away. Then she saw a small hill with a funny hump. \"What is over there?\" she wondered.","ko":"하나는 탐험가가 되고 싶었어요. 여름에 하나는 북쪽 마을에 사는 할아버지를 찾아갔어요. 할아버지 집 옆에는 넓은 농지가 있었어요. 하나는 긴 나뭇가지를 들고 들판을 가로질러 걸었어요. 멀리 굴뚝에서 연기가 나는 것이 보였어요. 그러다 툭 솟은 곳이 있는 작은 언덕을 보았어요. \"저기엔 뭐가 있을까?\" 하나는 궁금했어요.","questions":[{"q":"Where did Grandpa live?","options":["In a big city","In a northern town","On an island","Near the sea"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"\"she visited Grandpa in a northern town\" 할아버지는 북쪽 마을에 살았어요."},{"q":"Hana took a long \"stick.\" What is a stick here?","options":["A thin piece of wood","A toy car","A bag","A map"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"여기서 stick은 막대기, 나뭇가지를 뜻해요."}],"dictation":["Hana wanted to be an explorer.","His house was next to wide farmland."],"sents":["Hana wanted to be an explorer.","In summer, she visited Grandpa in a northern town.","His house was next to wide farmland.","Hana took a long stick and walked across the fields.","She saw smoke from a chimney far away.","Then she saw a small hill with a funny hump.","\"What is over there?\" she wondered."]},{"en":"Behind the hump, Hana found a shiny object in the grass. It was an old box. It did not seem broken. \"There may be a germ on it,\" she thought. \"I will wash my hands later.\" She brought the box home. Grandpa was deaf, so Hana wrote him a note. \"Look what I found!\" Grandpa smiled and gave her an extra cookie.","ko":"언덕 뒤에서 하나는 풀숲에 있는 반짝이는 물건을 발견했어요. 그건 오래된 상자였어요. 부서진 것 같지는 않았어요. \"세균이 있을지도 몰라.\" 하나는 생각했어요. \"나중에 손을 씻어야지.\" 하나는 상자를 집으로 가져왔어요. 할아버지는 귀가 들리지 않으셔서 하나는 쪽지를 썼어요. \"제가 뭘 찾았는지 보세요!\" 할아버지는 웃으며 하나에게 쿠키를 하나 더 주셨어요.","questions":[{"q":"Why did Hana write Grandpa a note?","options":["He was asleep","He was far away","He was deaf","He was busy"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"Grandpa was deaf\" 할아버지는 귀가 들리지 않아서 쪽지를 썼어요."},{"q":"Grandpa gave her an \"extra\" cookie. What does \"extra\" mean?","options":["Broken","Small","Old","One more than usual"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"extra는 추가의, 여분의라는 뜻이에요. 쿠키를 하나 더 준 거예요."}],"dictation":["It did not seem broken.","She brought the box home."],"sents":["Behind the hump, Hana found a shiny object in the grass.","It was an old box.","It did not seem broken.","\"There may be a germ on it,\" she thought.","\"I will wash my hands later.\" She brought the box home.","Grandpa was deaf, so Hana wrote him a note.","\"Look what I found!\" Grandpa smiled and gave her an extra cookie."]},{"en":"Inside the box was a small portrait of a young man. He wore a baseball shirt. \"That is me!\" Grandpa wrote. \"I played in a baseball league long ago.\" Hana's eyes were brilliant with joy. \"This is so meaningful,\" she said. Grandpa told her many stories with his hands and his notes.","ko":"상자 안에는 젊은 남자의 작은 인물 사진이 있었어요. 그는 야구 유니폼을 입고 있었어요. \"그건 나란다!\" 할아버지가 썼어요. \"오래전에 야구 리그에서 뛰었지.\" 하나의 눈이 기쁨으로 반짝였어요. \"정말 의미 있는 거네요.\" 하나가 말했어요. 할아버지는 손짓과 쪽지로 많은 이야기를 들려주셨어요.","questions":[{"q":"Who was the young man in the picture?","options":["Hana's dad","Grandpa","A famous singer","Hana's teacher"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"할아버지가 \"That is me!\"라고 썼어요. 사진 속 남자는 할아버지예요."},{"q":"What is a \"portrait\"?","options":["A picture of a person","A kind of food","A baseball bat","A long letter"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"portrait는 초상화, 인물 사진이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["He wore a baseball shirt.","I played in a baseball league long ago."],"sents":["Inside the box was a small portrait of a young man.","He wore a baseball shirt.","\"That is me!\" Grandpa wrote.","\"I played in a baseball league long ago.\" Hana's eyes were brilliant with joy.","\"This is so meaningful,\" she said.","Grandpa told her many stories with his hands and his notes."]},{"en":"Then Hana's little cousin Doyun took the portrait. He ran around the yard with it. Hana felt anger at first. But she saw his happy face and laughed. \"Anyway, he is just playing,\" she said. On her last day, Hana gave Grandpa a present. It was a new frame for the old photo. Grandpa hugged her tight.","ko":"그때 하나의 어린 사촌 도윤이가 그 사진을 가져갔어요. 도윤이는 사진을 들고 마당을 뛰어다녔어요. 하나는 처음엔 화가 났어요. 하지만 도윤이의 행복한 얼굴을 보고 웃었어요. \"어쨌든, 그냥 노는 거잖아.\" 하나가 말했어요. 마지막 날, 하나는 할아버지께 선물을 드렸어요. 그건 오래된 사진을 위한 새 액자였어요. 할아버지는 하나를 꼭 안아 주셨어요.","questions":[{"q":"What present did Hana give Grandpa?","options":["A cookie","A baseball","A new frame","A stick"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"It was a new frame for the old photo.\" 새 액자를 선물했어요."},{"q":"Hana felt \"anger\" at first. What is anger?","options":["Feeling sleepy","Feeling mad","Feeling hungry","Feeling cold"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"anger는 화, 분노라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["He ran around the yard with it.","On her last day, Hana gave Grandpa a present."],"sents":["Then Hana's little cousin Doyun took the portrait.","He ran around the yard with it.","Hana felt anger at first.","But she saw his happy face and laughed.","\"Anyway, he is just playing,\" she said.","On her last day, Hana gave Grandpa a present.","It was a new frame for the old photo.","Grandpa hugged her tight."]}]},{"key":11,"title":"Yuna's Dream Trip Poster","ids":["parental","upon","state","reality","accept","glue","anytime","softness","playful","achieve","thief","entrance","coral","beginning","else","online","view","successful","canyon","spine"],"parts":[{"en":"At the beginning of the week, Yuna's teacher gave a fun project. \"Make a poster about a dream trip.\" Yuna looked online with her mom. She found a big canyon in the state of Arizona. The view was amazing. She also found pictures of pink coral in the sea. \"I want to go to both!\" she said.","ko":"한 주가 시작될 때, 유나의 선생님이 재미있는 과제를 내 주셨어요. \"꿈의 여행에 대한 포스터를 만드세요.\" 유나는 엄마와 함께 인터넷을 찾아보았어요. 애리조나주에 있는 큰 협곡을 발견했어요. 경치가 정말 멋졌어요. 바다 속 분홍색 산호 사진도 찾았어요. \"두 곳 다 가고 싶어!\" 유나가 말했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What was the project about?","options":["A dream trip","A pet","A family","A favorite food"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"\"Make a poster about a dream trip.\" 꿈의 여행 포스터를 만드는 과제였어요."},{"q":"Yuna found a \"canyon.\" What is a canyon?","options":["A big city","A tall building","A deep valley with steep sides","A small lake"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"canyon은 협곡이에요. 양쪽이 가파른 깊은 골짜기예요."}],"dictation":["Yuna looked online with her mom.","She found a big canyon in the state of Arizona."],"sents":["At the beginning of the week, Yuna's teacher gave a fun project.","\"Make a poster about a dream trip.\" Yuna looked online with her mom.","She found a big canyon in the state of Arizona.","The view was amazing.","She also found pictures of pink coral in the sea.","\"I want to go to both!\" she said."]},{"en":"Yuna printed the pictures. She put glue on the back of each one. She placed them upon a big paper. Then her playful cat, Mochi, jumped on the table. He grabbed the coral picture and ran! \"Stop, little thief!\" Yuna laughed. She caught him and felt the softness of his fur.","ko":"유나는 사진들을 출력했어요. 사진마다 뒤에 풀을 발랐어요. 그리고 큰 종이 위에 붙였어요. 그때 장난기 많은 고양이 모찌가 탁자 위로 뛰어올랐어요. 모찌는 산호 사진을 물고 달아났어요! \"멈춰, 꼬마 도둑아!\" 유나가 웃었어요. 유나는 모찌를 잡고 부드러운 털을 느꼈어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Mochi take?","options":["The glue","The coral picture","A pencil","The canyon picture"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"\"He grabbed the coral picture and ran!\" 모찌는 산호 사진을 가져갔어요."},{"q":"Mochi is a \"playful\" cat. What does \"playful\" mean?","options":["Sleepy","Angry","Shy","Liking to play and have fun"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"playful은 장난기 많은이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["She put glue on the back of each one.","She placed them upon a big paper."],"sents":["Yuna printed the pictures.","She put glue on the back of each one.","She placed them upon a big paper.","Then her playful cat, Mochi, jumped on the table.","He grabbed the coral picture and ran!","\"Stop, little thief!\" Yuna laughed.","She caught him and felt the softness of his fur."]},{"en":"The coral picture had a fold down the middle, like a spine. \"Can I print something else?\" Yuna asked. But the printer was out of ink. She had to accept the folded picture. \"That is reality,\" Dad said with a smile. He signed the parental note for her project. \"It still looks good,\" he said.","ko":"산호 사진 한가운데에 척추처럼 접힌 자국이 생겼어요. \"다른 걸 출력해도 돼요?\" 유나가 물었어요. 하지만 프린터에 잉크가 없었어요. 유나는 접힌 사진을 받아들여야 했어요. \"그게 현실이란다.\" 아빠가 웃으며 말했어요. 아빠는 과제에 필요한 부모 확인서에 서명해 주셨어요. \"그래도 멋져 보여.\" 아빠가 말했어요.","questions":[{"q":"Why couldn't Yuna print a new picture?","options":["The printer was out of ink","Mochi broke it","It was too late","She had no paper"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"\"But the printer was out of ink.\" 프린터에 잉크가 없었어요."},{"q":"Yuna had to \"accept\" the folded picture. What does \"accept\" mean here?","options":["Throw away","Take and be okay with","Hide","Color"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"accept는 받아들이다라는 뜻이에요. 접힌 사진을 그대로 쓰기로 했어요."}],"dictation":["But the printer was out of ink.","He signed the parental note for her project."],"sents":["The coral picture had a fold down the middle, like a spine.","\"Can I print something else?\" Yuna asked.","But the printer was out of ink.","She had to accept the folded picture.","\"That is reality,\" Dad said with a smile.","He signed the parental note for her project.","\"It still looks good,\" he said."]},{"en":"The next day, Yuna stood at the entrance of her classroom. She held her poster up high. There were tiny paw prints from Mochi on it! Her friends loved them. The project was very successful. \"One day I will achieve my dream and visit these places,\" Yuna said. \"Until then, you can visit them online anytime,\" her teacher smiled.","ko":"다음 날, 유나는 교실 입구에 섰어요. 포스터를 높이 들었어요. 포스터에는 모찌의 작은 발자국도 찍혀 있었어요! 친구들은 그걸 무척 좋아했어요. 과제는 아주 성공적이었어요. \"언젠가 꿈을 이뤄서 이곳들에 갈 거야.\" 유나가 말했어요. \"그때까지는 언제든지 인터넷으로 가 볼 수 있지.\" 선생님이 웃으셨어요.","questions":[{"q":"What was on the poster that friends loved?","options":["Stickers","Glitter","Mochi's paw prints","A map"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"There were tiny paw prints from Mochi on it!\" 친구들은 발자국을 좋아했어요."},{"q":"Yuna stood at the \"entrance.\" What is an entrance?","options":["The roof","The window","The back wall","The way in, like a door"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"entrance는 입구라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["She held her poster up high.","The project was very successful."],"sents":["The next day, Yuna stood at the entrance of her classroom.","She held her poster up high.","There were tiny paw prints from Mochi on it!","Her friends loved them.","The project was very successful.","\"One day I will achieve my dream and visit these places,\" Yuna said.","\"Until then, you can visit them online anytime,\" her teacher smiled."]}]},{"key":12,"title":"Jiwoo and the Little Brown Horse","ids":["plain","flesh","barely","snap","historical","toward","cast","include","receive","device","grab","supper","hometown","string","beg","solve","completely","basis","choice","stable"],"parts":[{"en":"Jiwoo fell off her bike last week. She heard a snap, and her arm hurt. Now she had a cast on it. She could barely write. On Saturday, her family visited Grandma's hometown. There was an old historical farm there. It had a big red stable full of horses.","ko":"지우는 지난주에 자전거에서 넘어졌어요. 딱 하는 소리가 나더니 팔이 아팠어요. 이제 지우의 팔에는 깁스가 있었어요. 지우는 글씨를 거의 쓸 수 없었어요. 토요일에 가족은 할머니의 고향을 찾아갔어요. 그곳에는 오래된 역사적인 농장이 있었어요. 농장에는 말들로 가득한 커다란 빨간 마구간이 있었어요.","questions":[{"q":"Where did Jiwoo's family go on Saturday?","options":["To the beach","To Grandma's hometown","To a zoo","To school"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"\"her family visited Grandma's hometown\" 할머니의 고향에 갔어요."},{"q":"Jiwoo had a \"cast\" on her arm. What is a cast here?","options":["A hard cover that helps a broken bone heal","A watch","A bracelet","A glove"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"여기서 cast는 깁스를 뜻해요."}],"dictation":["Jiwoo fell off her bike last week.","It had a big red stable full of horses."],"sents":["Jiwoo fell off her bike last week.","She heard a snap, and her arm hurt.","Now she had a cast on it.","She could barely write.","On Saturday, her family visited Grandma's hometown.","There was an old historical farm there.","It had a big red stable full of horses."]},{"en":"A small brown horse walked toward Jiwoo. It looked plain, with no spots. But it had kind eyes. Jiwoo wanted to grab its rope with her good hand. A farmer tied a string with a bell on its neck. \"Please, can I ride it?\" Jiwoo began to beg. \"Not with a cast,\" Mom said.","ko":"작은 갈색 말이 지우 쪽으로 걸어왔어요. 점 하나 없이 평범해 보였어요. 하지만 눈이 다정했어요. 지우는 다치지 않은 손으로 말의 밧줄을 붙잡고 싶었어요. 농부가 말의 목에 방울 달린 끈을 묶었어요. \"제발, 타 봐도 돼요?\" 지우가 조르기 시작했어요. \"깁스를 하고는 안 돼.\" 엄마가 말했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did the farmer tie on the horse's neck?","options":["A ribbon","A hat","A string with a bell","A flower"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"A farmer tied a string with a bell on its neck.\" 방울 달린 끈을 묶었어요."},{"q":"Jiwoo began to \"beg.\" What does \"beg\" mean?","options":["To sing","To ask again and again","To cry","To sleep"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"beg는 간청하다, 조르다라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["A small brown horse walked toward Jiwoo.","It looked plain, with no spots."],"sents":["A small brown horse walked toward Jiwoo.","It looked plain, with no spots.","But it had kind eyes.","Jiwoo wanted to grab its rope with her good hand.","A farmer tied a string with a bell on its neck.","\"Please, can I ride it?\" Jiwoo began to beg.","\"Not with a cast,\" Mom said."]},{"en":"Jiwoo was sad. The farmer gave her a choice. \"You can feed the horse or brush it.\" She chose to feed it. The snack would include carrots and a peach. Grandma cut the soft flesh of the peach. The horse loved it! The farmer showed her a device. \"It helps me solve a big problem. It tells me when the horses are hungry.\"","ko":"지우는 슬펐어요. 농부가 지우에게 선택권을 주었어요. \"말에게 먹이를 주거나 빗질을 해 줄 수 있단다.\" 지우는 먹이 주기를 골랐어요. 간식에는 당근과 복숭아가 포함되었어요. 할머니가 복숭아의 부드러운 과육을 잘라 주셨어요. 말은 그걸 정말 좋아했어요! 농부가 지우에게 기기 하나를 보여 주었어요. \"이건 큰 문제를 해결하도록 도와준단다. 말들이 언제 배고픈지 알려 주거든.\"","questions":[{"q":"What did Jiwoo choose to do?","options":["Feed the horse","Brush the horse","Ride the horse","Go home"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"\"She chose to feed it.\" 지우는 먹이 주기를 골랐어요."},{"q":"What does \"flesh\" mean in \"the soft flesh of the peach\"?","options":["The seed","The leaf","The box","The soft part you eat"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"여기서 flesh는 과육, 즉 먹는 부드러운 부분이에요."}],"dictation":["The farmer gave her a choice.","The snack would include carrots and a peach."],"sents":["Jiwoo was sad.","The farmer gave her a choice.","\"You can feed the horse or brush it.\" She chose to feed it.","The snack would include carrots and a peach.","Grandma cut the soft flesh of the peach.","The horse loved it!","The farmer showed her a device.","\"It helps me solve a big problem.","It tells me when the horses are hungry.\""]},{"en":"\"I feed the horses on a daily basis,\" the farmer said. \"Come back and help me when your arm is better.\" Jiwoo was so happy to receive his invitation. At supper, she told Grandma everything. \"My arm hurts, but today was completely perfect!\" she said. That night, she dreamed about the little brown horse.","ko":"\"나는 매일 말들에게 먹이를 준단다.\" 농부가 말했어요. \"팔이 나으면 다시 와서 도와주렴.\" 지우는 초대를 받아서 무척 기뻤어요. 저녁 식사 때, 지우는 할머니께 모든 걸 이야기했어요. \"팔은 아프지만 오늘은 완전히 완벽했어요!\" 지우가 말했어요. 그날 밤, 지우는 작은 갈색 말 꿈을 꾸었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Jiwoo dream about?","options":["Her bike","Her school","The little brown horse","A big cake"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"she dreamed about the little brown horse\" 작은 갈색 말 꿈을 꾸었어요."},{"q":"At \"supper,\" Jiwoo told Grandma everything. What is supper?","options":["Breakfast","The evening meal","A snack at school","A game"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"supper는 저녁 식사라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Jiwoo was so happy to receive his invitation.","At supper, she told Grandma everything."],"sents":["\"I feed the horses on a daily basis,\" the farmer said.","\"Come back and help me when your arm is better.\" Jiwoo was so happy to receive his invitation.","At supper, she told Grandma everything.","\"My arm hurts, but today was completely perfect!\" she said.","That night, she dreamed about the little brown horse."]}]},{"key":13,"title":"Dahee Runs for Gold","ids":["rotten","textbook","terrible","solid","clearly","stare","protein","suffer","ton","medal","enemy","bit","if","overseas","cause","practice","lifestyle","oak","roast","purchase"],"parts":[{"en":"Dahee wanted a medal in the school race. She started to practice every morning. She also changed her lifestyle. She ate eggs and beans for protein. Her science textbook said protein makes muscles strong. \"If I eat well and run every day, I can win,\" she said to herself.","ko":"다희는 학교 달리기 대회에서 메달을 따고 싶었어요. 매일 아침 연습을 시작했어요. 생활 방식도 바꾸었어요. 단백질을 먹으려고 달걀과 콩을 먹었어요. 과학 교과서에 단백질이 근육을 튼튼하게 한다고 쓰여 있었거든요. \"만약 잘 먹고 매일 달리면 이길 수 있어.\" 다희는 혼잣말을 했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Dahee want?","options":["A new bike","A medal","A puppy","A book"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"\"Dahee wanted a medal in the school race.\" 메달을 원했어요."},{"q":"What is a \"textbook\"?","options":["A book you study with at school","A phone message","A comic book","A notebook for drawing"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"textbook은 교과서라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["She started to practice every morning.","She ate eggs and beans for protein."],"sents":["Dahee wanted a medal in the school race.","She started to practice every morning.","She also changed her lifestyle.","She ate eggs and beans for protein.","Her science textbook said protein makes muscles strong.","\"If I eat well and run every day, I can win,\" she said to herself."]},{"en":"One day, Dahee ran past a big oak tree. She saw an apple on the ground. It was rotten and brown. It smelled terrible! Dahee laughed and ran on. But a bit later, she tripped on a root. Her knee hurt a little. She did not want to suffer more, so she rested for two days.","ko":"어느 날, 다희는 커다란 참나무 옆을 달려 지나갔어요. 땅에 사과 하나가 떨어져 있었어요. 썩어서 갈색이었어요. 냄새가 끔찍했어요! 다희는 웃으며 계속 달렸어요. 하지만 조금 후에 나무뿌리에 걸려 넘어졌어요. 무릎이 조금 아팠어요. 더 아프고 싶지 않아서 다희는 이틀 동안 쉬었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Dahee trip on?","options":["A rock","An apple","A root","Her shoe"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"she tripped on a root\" 나무뿌리에 걸려 넘어졌어요."},{"q":"The apple was \"rotten.\" What does \"rotten\" mean?","options":["Fresh and sweet","Very big","Bright red","Old and bad to eat"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"rotten은 썩은이라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["One day, Dahee ran past a big oak tree.","But a bit later, she tripped on a root."],"sents":["One day, Dahee ran past a big oak tree.","She saw an apple on the ground.","It was rotten and brown.","It smelled terrible!","Dahee laughed and ran on.","But a bit later, she tripped on a root.","Her knee hurt a little.","She did not want to suffer more, so she rested for two days."]},{"en":"Her uncle lived overseas in Canada. He called her. \"I will purchase new running shoes for you!\" A week later, a box came. The shoes were light but solid. \"I can run a ton of laps in these!\" Dahee said. That night, Mom made roast chicken. \"Being too tired can cause problems. Rest is not your enemy,\" Mom said.","ko":"다희의 삼촌은 해외인 캐나다에 살았어요. 삼촌이 전화를 했어요. \"새 운동화를 사 줄게!\" 일주일 후에 상자가 도착했어요. 운동화는 가볍지만 튼튼했어요. \"이걸 신으면 아주 많이 달릴 수 있겠어!\" 다희가 말했어요. 그날 밤 엄마는 구운 닭고기를 만들어 주셨어요. \"너무 지치면 문제가 생길 수 있어. 휴식은 너의 적이 아니란다.\" 엄마가 말했어요.","questions":[{"q":"Who bought Dahee new shoes?","options":["Her uncle","Her mom","Her teacher","Her friend"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"캐나다에 사는 삼촌이 \"I will purchase new running shoes for you!\"라고 했어요."},{"q":"Her uncle lived \"overseas.\" What does \"overseas\" mean?","options":["Next door","In another country across the sea","Under the sea","At school"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"overseas는 해외에라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Her uncle lived overseas in Canada.","The shoes were light but solid."],"sents":["Her uncle lived overseas in Canada.","He called her.","\"I will purchase new running shoes for you!\" A week later, a box came.","The shoes were light but solid.","\"I can run a ton of laps in these!\" Dahee said.","That night, Mom made roast chicken.","\"Being too tired can cause problems.","Rest is not your enemy,\" Mom said."]},{"en":"On race day, Dahee stood at the starting line. Other kids began to stare at her shiny new shoes. \"Ready, go!\" She ran fast. She could clearly hear her family cheering. Dahee came in first! She got a gold medal. She looked at it for a long time. \"Practice really works,\" she said with a big smile.","ko":"대회 날, 다희는 출발선에 섰어요. 다른 아이들이 다희의 반짝이는 새 운동화를 빤히 쳐다보기 시작했어요. \"준비, 출발!\" 다희는 빠르게 달렸어요. 가족들이 응원하는 소리가 또렷하게 들렸어요. 다희가 1등으로 들어왔어요! 금메달을 받았어요. 다희는 메달을 오랫동안 바라보았어요. \"연습은 정말 효과가 있어.\" 다희는 활짝 웃으며 말했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What place did Dahee get in the race?","options":["Last","Third","First","Second"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"Dahee came in first!\" 1등을 했어요."},{"q":"The kids began to \"stare\" at her shoes. What does \"stare\" mean?","options":["Kick","Laugh","Run away","Look at for a long time"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"stare는 빤히 쳐다보다라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["On race day, Dahee stood at the starting line.","She could clearly hear her family cheering."],"sents":["On race day, Dahee stood at the starting line.","Other kids began to stare at her shiny new shoes.","\"Ready, go!\" She ran fast.","She could clearly hear her family cheering.","Dahee came in first!","She got a gold medal.","She looked at it for a long time.","\"Practice really works,\" she said with a big smile."]}]},{"key":14,"title":"Sora and Bobo the Seal","ids":["differently","seal","national","award","usual","celebrate","capture","bloody","pale","main","neat","circus","bathe","total","male","direct","relate","deal","private","progress"],"parts":[{"en":"Sora loved taking photos. One day, she saw a poster for a national photo contest. The award was a new camera! \"I will capture something special,\" Sora said. On Sunday, she went to the zoo with her dad. Her main plan was to take a photo of a male seal named Bobo.","ko":"소라는 사진 찍는 것을 좋아했어요. 어느 날, 전국 사진 대회 포스터를 보았어요. 상품은 새 카메라였어요! \"특별한 걸 사진에 담을 거야.\" 소라가 말했어요. 일요일에 소라는 아빠와 동물원에 갔어요. 소라의 가장 중요한 계획은 보보라는 수컷 물개의 사진을 찍는 것이었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What was the award for the contest?","options":["A new camera","A trip","A bike","A seal toy"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"\"The award was a new camera!\" 상품은 새 카메라였어요."},{"q":"Bobo is a \"male\" seal. What does \"male\" mean?","options":["Baby","Boy (not girl)","Very old","Sick"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"male은 남성의, 수컷의라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["One day, she saw a poster for a national photo contest.","On Sunday, she went to the zoo with her dad."],"sents":["Sora loved taking photos.","One day, she saw a poster for a national photo contest.","The award was a new camera!","\"I will capture something special,\" Sora said.","On Sunday, she went to the zoo with her dad.","Her main plan was to take a photo of a male seal named Bobo."]},{"en":"But Bobo was not in his usual spot. \"Where is he?\" Sora asked. A zookeeper smiled. \"He is in the pool. It is time to bathe.\" Bobo splashed and spun like a circus star. He clapped his flippers. \"That is neat!\" Sora said. She tried to take the photo differently, from down low.","ko":"하지만 보보는 평소 있던 자리에 없었어요. \"보보는 어디 있어요?\" 소라가 물었어요. 사육사가 웃었어요. \"수영장에 있단다. 목욕할 시간이거든.\" 보보는 서커스 스타처럼 물을 튀기며 빙글빙글 돌았어요. 지느러미로 박수도 쳤어요. \"멋지다!\" 소라가 말했어요. 소라는 낮은 곳에서 다르게 사진을 찍어 보았어요.","questions":[{"q":"Where was Bobo?","options":["In his house","Asleep on a rock","In the pool","At the circus"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"He is in the pool. It is time to bathe.\" 보보는 수영장에 있었어요."},{"q":"It was time for Bobo to \"bathe.\" What does \"bathe\" mean?","options":["Eat","Sleep","Sing","Wash in water"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"bathe는 목욕하다라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["But Bobo was not in his usual spot.","Bobo splashed and spun like a circus star."],"sents":["But Bobo was not in his usual spot.","\"Where is he?\" Sora asked.","A zookeeper smiled.","\"He is in the pool.","It is time to bathe.\" Bobo splashed and spun like a circus star.","He clapped his flippers.","\"That is neat!\" Sora said.","She tried to take the photo differently, from down low."]},{"en":"Suddenly, Sora slipped on the wet floor. She got a bloody nose! Her face looked pale. The zookeeper took her to a private room. He gave her a tissue and some water. \"I slipped here last week too,\" he laughed. Sora could relate to him. Then he showed her a direct path back to the seal pool.","ko":"갑자기 소라가 젖은 바닥에서 미끄러졌어요. 코피가 났어요! 소라의 얼굴이 창백해 보였어요. 사육사는 소라를 개인 방으로 데려갔어요. 휴지와 물을 주었어요. \"나도 지난주에 여기서 미끄러졌단다.\" 사육사가 웃었어요. 소라는 사육사의 마음에 공감할 수 있었어요. 그런 다음 사육사는 물개 수영장으로 곧장 가는 길을 알려 주었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did the zookeeper give Sora?","options":["A tissue and some water","A camera","A fish","Ice cream"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"\"He gave her a tissue and some water.\" 휴지와 물을 주었어요."},{"q":"Her face looked \"pale.\" What does \"pale\" mean here?","options":["Very red","White, with less color","Dirty","Happy"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"pale은 창백한이라는 뜻이에요. 얼굴빛이 하얗게 된 거예요."}],"dictation":["Suddenly, Sora slipped on the wet floor.","The zookeeper took her to a private room."],"sents":["Suddenly, Sora slipped on the wet floor.","She got a bloody nose!","Her face looked pale.","The zookeeper took her to a private room.","He gave her a tissue and some water.","\"I slipped here last week too,\" he laughed.","Sora could relate to him.","Then he showed her a direct path back to the seal pool."]},{"en":"Sora took a total of fifty photos. Her progress was slow, but one photo was perfect. Bobo was smiling at the camera! A month later, she won the award. \"What a great deal! One photo, one new camera,\" Dad joked. They went out for ice cream to celebrate. Sora sent Bobo a thank-you card too.","ko":"소라는 모두 합해서 사진 50장을 찍었어요. 진행은 느렸지만 한 장은 완벽했어요. 보보가 카메라를 보고 웃고 있었거든요! 한 달 후, 소라는 상을 받았어요. \"정말 좋은 거래구나! 사진 한 장에 새 카메라 하나라니.\" 아빠가 농담했어요. 가족은 축하하려고 아이스크림을 먹으러 갔어요. 소라는 보보에게도 감사 카드를 보냈어요.","questions":[{"q":"How many photos did Sora take?","options":["Five","Fifteen","Fifty","One hundred"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"Sora took a total of fifty photos.\" 모두 50장을 찍었어요."},{"q":"They went out to \"celebrate.\" What does \"celebrate\" mean?","options":["To clean up","To say sorry","To go to sleep","To have fun because something good happened"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"celebrate는 축하하다라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Sora took a total of fifty photos.","They went out for ice cream to celebrate."],"sents":["Sora took a total of fifty photos.","Her progress was slow, but one photo was perfect.","Bobo was smiling at the camera!","A month later, she won the award.","\"What a great deal!","One photo, one new camera,\" Dad joked.","They went out for ice cream to celebrate.","Sora sent Bobo a thank-you card too."]}]},{"key":15,"title":"Eunbi Fixes the Helicopter","ids":["spot","about","beside","repair","laziness","burner","steak","peace","lonely","record","delete","rude","teen","motor","helicopter","connect","sight","sprinkle","sense","prefer"],"parts":[{"en":"Eunbi had a teen brother named Taemin. He had an old toy helicopter. Its motor was broken. \"Can you repair it?\" Eunbi asked. \"Maybe later,\" Taemin said and lay on the sofa. Eunbi sighed at his laziness. She felt a little lonely. She wanted to play with him.","ko":"은비에게는 태민이라는 십 대 오빠가 있었어요. 오빠에게는 오래된 장난감 헬리콥터가 있었어요. 헬리콥터의 모터가 고장 났어요. \"그거 고칠 수 있어?\" 은비가 물었어요. \"나중에.\" 태민이는 그렇게 말하고 소파에 누웠어요. 은비는 오빠의 게으름에 한숨을 쉬었어요. 은비는 조금 외로웠어요. 오빠랑 놀고 싶었거든요.","questions":[{"q":"What was broken on the toy helicopter?","options":["The door","The motor","The wheels","The light"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"\"Its motor was broken.\" 모터가 고장 났어요."},{"q":"Eunbi asked, \"Can you repair it?\" What does \"repair\" mean?","options":["Fix","Buy","Paint","Throw"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"repair는 수리하다, 고치다라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["He had an old toy helicopter.","Eunbi sighed at his laziness."],"sents":["Eunbi had a teen brother named Taemin.","He had an old toy helicopter.","Its motor was broken.","\"Can you repair it?\" Eunbi asked.","\"Maybe later,\" Taemin said and lay on the sofa.","Eunbi sighed at his laziness.","She felt a little lonely.","She wanted to play with him."]},{"en":"Eunbi sat beside him with the helicopter. \"Please tell me about motors,\" she said. Taemin sat up. \"Okay. First, we connect these two wires.\" Eunbi used her phone to record a video of each step. \"Now it makes sense!\" she said. Taemin smiled. He was enjoying it too.","ko":"은비는 헬리콥터를 들고 오빠 옆에 앉았어요. \"모터에 대해 알려 줘.\" 은비가 말했어요. 태민이가 일어나 앉았어요. \"좋아. 먼저 이 두 전선을 연결하는 거야.\" 은비는 휴대폰으로 단계마다 영상을 녹화했어요. \"이제 이해가 돼!\" 은비가 말했어요. 태민이가 웃었어요. 오빠도 즐거워하고 있었어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Eunbi use her phone for?","options":["To call Mom","To play a game","To record a video","To listen to music"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"Eunbi used her phone to record a video of each step.\" 영상을 녹화했어요."},{"q":"Eunbi sat \"beside\" him. What does \"beside\" mean?","options":["Far from","On top of","Behind","Next to"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"beside는 ~옆에라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["Eunbi sat beside him with the helicopter.","First, we connect these two wires."],"sents":["Eunbi sat beside him with the helicopter.","\"Please tell me about motors,\" she said.","Taemin sat up.","\"Okay.","First, we connect these two wires.\" Eunbi used her phone to record a video of each step.","\"Now it makes sense!\" she said.","Taemin smiled.","He was enjoying it too."]},{"en":"Oops! Eunbi almost deleted the video by mistake. \"Hey, don't!\" Taemin shouted. Then he said, \"Sorry, that was rude.\" They looked for the last loose wire. Eunbi found the spot first. \"You have good sight!\" Taemin said. \"Do you prefer red or blue tape?\" \"Blue!\" Eunbi said.","ko":"앗! 은비가 실수로 영상을 지울 뻔했어요. \"야, 안 돼!\" 태민이가 소리쳤어요. 그러고는 \"미안, 무례하게 굴었네.\"라고 말했어요. 둘은 마지막 헐거운 전선을 찾았어요. 은비가 먼저 그 자리를 발견했어요. \"너 시력 좋다!\" 태민이가 말했어요. \"빨간 테이프가 좋아, 파란 테이프가 좋아?\" \"파란색!\" 은비가 말했어요.","questions":[{"q":"Who found the loose wire first?","options":["Eunbi","Taemin","Dad","Mom"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"\"Eunbi found the spot first.\" 은비가 먼저 찾았어요."},{"q":"Taemin said, \"That was rude.\" What does \"rude\" mean?","options":["Very kind","Not polite","Very funny","Really fast"],"answer":1,"why_ko":"rude는 무례한이라는 뜻이에요. 소리친 것을 사과한 거예요."}],"dictation":["Eunbi almost deleted the video by mistake.","They looked for the last loose wire."],"sents":["Oops!","Eunbi almost deleted the video by mistake.","\"Hey, don't!\" Taemin shouted.","Then he said, \"Sorry, that was rude.\" They looked for the last loose wire.","Eunbi found the spot first.","\"You have good sight!\" Taemin said.","\"Do you prefer red or blue tape?\" \"Blue!\" Eunbi said."]},{"en":"The helicopter flew up into the air! Eunbi and Taemin cheered. Then Dad called them for dinner. He was cooking steak on the burner. \"Can I sprinkle the salt?\" Eunbi asked. They ate together and laughed. After dinner, the house was full of peace. Eunbi was not lonely anymore.","ko":"헬리콥터가 하늘로 날아올랐어요! 은비와 태민이는 환호했어요. 그때 아빠가 저녁 먹으라고 불렀어요. 아빠는 버너에서 스테이크를 굽고 있었어요. \"제가 소금 뿌려도 돼요?\" 은비가 물었어요. 가족은 함께 먹으며 웃었어요. 저녁 식사 후, 집 안은 평온함으로 가득했어요. 은비는 더 이상 외롭지 않았어요.","questions":[{"q":"What was Dad cooking?","options":["Soup","Noodles","Steak","Pancakes"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"He was cooking steak on the burner.\" 스테이크를 굽고 있었어요."},{"q":"Eunbi asked to \"sprinkle\" the salt. What does \"sprinkle\" mean?","options":["Eat it all","Hide it","Wash it","Drop little bits on top"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"sprinkle은 뿌리다라는 뜻이에요."}],"dictation":["He was cooking steak on the burner.","After dinner, the house was full of peace."],"sents":["The helicopter flew up into the air!","Eunbi and Taemin cheered.","Then Dad called them for dinner.","He was cooking steak on the burner.","\"Can I sprinkle the salt?\" Eunbi asked.","They ate together and laughed.","After dinner, the house was full of peace.","Eunbi was not lonely anymore."]}]},{"key":16,"title":"Haeun's True or False Game","ids":["sentence","pleasure","false","attention","purpose"],"parts":[{"en":"Haeun's class had a fun game called True or False. The teacher wrote a sentence on the board. \"Cats can fly.\" Everyone laughed. \"False!\" Haeun shouted. \"Good!\" said the teacher. \"Now pay attention. Here is the next one.\" Haeun sat up straight. She did not want to miss anything.","ko":"하은이네 반은 '참일까 거짓일까'라는 재미있는 게임을 했어요. 선생님이 칠판에 문장 하나를 쓰셨어요. \"고양이는 날 수 있다.\" 모두 웃었어요. \"거짓!\" 하은이가 외쳤어요. \"잘했어!\" 선생님이 말씀하셨어요. \"이제 집중하세요. 다음 문제예요.\" 하은이는 허리를 곧게 펴고 앉았어요. 하나도 놓치고 싶지 않았거든요.","questions":[{"q":"What did the teacher write on the board first?","options":["Dogs can swim.","Cats can fly.","Fish can sing.","Birds can read."],"answer":1,"why_ko":"선생님이 처음 쓴 문장은 \"Cats can fly.\"였어요."},{"q":"Haeun shouted \"False!\" What does \"false\" mean?","options":["Not true","Very funny","Too hard","Correct"],"answer":0,"why_ko":"false는 틀린, 거짓의라는 뜻이에요. 고양이는 날 수 없으니까요."}],"dictation":["The teacher wrote a sentence on the board.","She did not want to miss anything."],"sents":["Haeun's class had a fun game called True or False.","The teacher wrote a sentence on the board.","\"Cats can fly.\" Everyone laughed.","\"False!\" Haeun shouted.","\"Good!\" said the teacher.","\"Now pay attention.","Here is the next one.\" Haeun sat up straight.","She did not want to miss anything."]},{"en":"The next sentence was \"Octopuses have three hearts.\" Nobody was sure. Haeun thought hard. \"True!\" she said. She was right! At the end, the teacher explained the purpose of the game. \"It helps us think carefully,\" she said. Haeun won a sticker. \"It was my pleasure to play,\" she said with a smile.","ko":"다음 문장은 \"문어는 심장이 세 개다.\"였어요. 아무도 확신하지 못했어요. 하은이는 곰곰이 생각했어요. \"참!\" 하은이가 말했어요. 하은이가 맞았어요! 마지막에 선생님은 게임의 목적을 설명해 주셨어요. \"이 게임은 우리가 신중하게 생각하도록 도와줘요.\" 선생님이 말씀하셨어요. 하은이는 스티커를 받았어요. \"게임을 해서 즐거웠어요.\" 하은이가 웃으며 말했어요.","questions":[{"q":"What did Haeun win?","options":["A pencil","A book","A sticker","A candy"],"answer":2,"why_ko":"\"Haeun won a sticker.\" 스티커를 받았어요."},{"q":"The teacher explained the \"purpose\" of the game. What is a purpose?","options":["The name","The winner","The time","The reason for doing it"],"answer":3,"why_ko":"purpose는 목적이라는 뜻이에요. 게임을 하는 이유를 설명한 거예요."}],"dictation":["At the end, the teacher explained the purpose of the game.","It was my pleasure to play"],"sents":["The next sentence was \"Octopuses have three hearts.\" Nobody was sure.","Haeun thought hard.","\"True!\" she said.","She was right!","At the end, the teacher explained the purpose of the game.","\"It helps us think carefully,\" she said.","Haeun won a sticker.","\"It was my pleasure to play,\" she said with a smile."]}]}];
